PVD("papua_new_guinea_ndp_2018-2022",{"docs":["","PNG NDP 2018 22 Vol I","PNG NDP 2018 22 Vol II"],"s":{"1":[[1,"11","4","Reliable and Cost-Efficient Power Generation and Transmission Investment","Furthermore, the Government is investing in more reliable and cost-efficient models of power generation and transmission of electricity to reduce cost for businesses and people.",""],[1,"11","5","Rural Electrification Program","The MTDP III will focus on the following district programs: district hospitals, district offices, district town water supply systems, district town roads upgrading and sealing, and rural electrification program.",""],[1,"39","1","Clean Energy Generation Investment","More investment in clean energy generation, such as hydro, solar, wind, biomass and geothermal power generation will be accelerated to reduce dependence on diesel power generation.",""],[1,"50","2","Electricity Supply Expansion and Grid Extension","Reliable and affordable Electricity supply to households and for industrial use will be expanded with increase in power generation including renewable energy and extension of main grid throughout the country.",""],[1,"51","9","National Electricity Supply Rollout Plan","Increase electricity supply with extension of transmission power grid on to communities through National Electricity Supply Roll out Plan.",""],[1,"51","10","Sustainable Energy Supply Expansion","Increase supply of energy with sustainable energy source.",""],[1,"53","2","National Rural Electrification Rollout Program","National Rural Electrification Roll out Program",""],[1,"53","4","Towns Electrification Investment Program","PNG Towns Electrification Investment Program",""],[1,"53","5","Rural and Urban Electricity Supply Expansion","To improve and expand reliable supply of electricity in Towns throughout the country.",""],[1,"77","4","Electrification, Water Supply and Communication Services Investment","Electrification, water supply and communication services will be duly funded with allocation of K2 billion or 8% of total capital expenditure",""]],"2":[[2,"72","3","Electricity Sector Liberalization and Restructuring","The electricity industry needs to liberalize its business to encourage proper competition into transmission, generation and wholesaling/retailing.",""],[2,"72","3","Transmission Infrastructure Prioritization","Government will prioritise on transmission infrastructure, while allowing for the private sector to compete in generation and retailing.",""],[2,"72","3","National Energy Authority and Electricity Regulation Commission Establishment","Creation of a National Energy Authority and Electricity Regulation Commission are needed to facilitate and regulate these restructures.",""],[2,"72","3","National Energy Policy Formulation","Furthermore, a National Energy Policy needs to be formulated to ensure that these interventions are implemented as a priority under MTDP III.",""],[2,"73","11","National Energy Policy and Regulatory Framework","Formulate National Energy Policy and regulatory framework",""],[2,"73","12","Electricity Supply and Distribution Regulatory Framework","Create regulatory framework for electricity supply and distribution",""],[2,"73","14","Sustainable Energy Policy Development","Introduce specific sustainable energy policies",""],[2,"73","15","Sustainable Energy Supply Investment","Increase investment in sustainable energy supply options",""],[2,"73","16","Power Transmission Line and Infrastructure Improvement","Improve power transmission lines and infrastructure to reduce loss of power supply",""],[2,"73","18","Establish National Energy Authority and Implement NEROP","Establish National Energy Authority and implement NEROP",""],[2,"73","21","Power Transmission Infrastructure and Grid Improvement","Improve power transmission infrastructure and grids",""],[2,"73","26","Towns Electrification Investment Program","PNG Towns Electrification Investment Program",""]],"3":[[1,"17","2","Citizen Wealth Creation Support Measures","Under the MTDP III, the Government will focus on: (4) improving and increasing opportunities for citizens to create wealth,",""],[1,"17","2","Public Goods and Services Delivery Improvement","Under the MTDP III, the Government will focus on: (5) improving the quality and effectiveness in the delivery of public goods and services.",""],[1,"21","2","Business Environment Improvement and SME Support Measures","The Government's effort to develop infrastructure, unlock the land for business, secure state equity financing, and resolve law and order issues will result in reducing the cost of doing business in PNG.",""],[1,"36","2","Small and Medium Enterprises Policy","The MTDP III aims to address sustainable, equitable and inclusive growth by better understanding of potentials of each region and/or province and the needs of vulnerable and disadvantaged groups, through deliberate policy interventions, such as the Small and Medium Enterprises (SME) Policy.",""],[1,"40","1","Public-Private Partnership Strengthening for SOE Performance","Over the next five years (2018-2022), the target will be to reinforce the public-private partnerships (PPP) to improve efficiency and overall performance of the SOEs, with the overarching objective of delivering goods and services to improve livelihoods across the country at high quality and affordable prices.",""],[1,"40","11","Financial Inclusion and Credit Facilitation Strategy","An effective financial inclusion and credit facilitation strategy is needed.",""],[1,"40","12","Financial Inclusion Services Expansion","The Government encourages financial and non-financial institutions and development partners and stakeholders to expand their financial inclusion services.",""],[1,"41","4","SME Development and Market Linkage Support","The SME Policy will continue to promote the development of small to medium enterprises, in particular, the strengthening of the linkages between SMEs and larger industries and investors, as well as regional and international markets and the transfer and adoption of appropriate technology to boost efficiency and productivity of domestic producers.",""],[1,"44","10","Bankable Land Expansion for Productive Use","Increase bankable land for productive utilisation to unlock its economic potential and engage land-owners in the formal market.",""],[1,"46","9","Citizen Empowerment for Majority SME Ownership","The Government is determined to reverse this situation by implementing a deliberate strategy to empower PNG citizens and support them take majority ownership of the SME sector.",""],[1,"48","22","Credit Guarantee Corporation Establishment","Establish Credit Guarantee Corporation by 2019, to assist PNG citizens who do not have collateral to obtain loans to be able to start up new businesses.",""],[1,"48","23","Business Incubation Centres for SMEs","15. Establish Business Incubation Centres for SMEs.",""],[1,"76","3","SME Sector Promotion and Expansion","MTDP III focuses on promoting and expanding SME sector and developing agriculture and agri-business in the medium term.",""],[1,"81","2","SME, Trade, and Growth Sector Expansion Initiative","The key investments will be in agriculture, livestock, fisheries, forestry, transport and infrastructure, small and medium enterprises, expansion of trade and other growth areas.",""],[1,"81","4","Support for Provincial and District Economic Self-Reliance","Provinces and districts must be fully supported in their efforts for economic stability and self-reliance.",""],[1,"81","4","Provincial and District Investment Identification Mechanism","MTDP III emphasizes an increasing role of the provincial and district governments in identifying viable investment options for creating employment and income opportunities for their constituents.",""],[1,"84","4","SME Policy Implementation Support","The Government expects them to support the implementation of our key development policies and Strategies such as SME Policy to realize a greater share of our wealth for our citizens.",""],[2,"34","13","SME Financial Access and Incentives Support","Provide financial access and incentives for national SMEs in manufacturing sector.",""],[2,"34","14","SME Manufacturing Tax Incentive Scheme","Provide tax incentives for national SMEs engaged in manufacturing.",""],[2,"35","2","SME Policy Implementation and Sector Development Programme","The Government plans to achieve these objectives by implementing the SME Policy, especially the key areas of entrepreneurial development, legislative framework, catalyst projects, infrastructure development, and integrated coordination structure.",""],[2,"35","2","National Reserve Business Policy for SME Participation","The next five years will see the implementation of the National Reserve Business Policy to achieve 100% national participation in the SME sector, particularly Increase in women participation in SME, and the establishment of microfinance banking services in all provincial headquarters for SMEs to have access to credits.",""],[2,"35","3","Incubation Centres Development","Major investments such as the development of incubation centres, special economic zones, and SMEs access to credit facilities among other priorities will be pursued in the medium to grow the economy.",""],[2,"35","3","Special Economic Zones Development","Major investments such as the development of incubation centres, special economic zones, and SMEs access to credit facilities among other priorities will be pursued in the medium to grow the economy.",""],[2,"35","3","SME Credit Access Facility","Major investments such as the development of incubation centres, special economic zones, and SMEs access to credit facilities among other priorities will be pursued in the medium to grow the economy.",""],[2,"36","17","MSME Registration Awareness Campaign","Create awareness on registering MSMEs",""],[2,"36","18","Regional SME Training Centres","Establishment of 4 regional SME training centres",""],[2,"36","19","SME Incentive Support for Nationals","Provide incentive for nationals to venture into SMEs",""],[2,"36","20","Enabling Infrastructure for National SME Growth","Provide enabling infrastructure for national SMEs to grow",""],[2,"36","21","Financial Access Enabling Environment","Create a conducive and flexible environment for all to access finance",""],[2,"36","22","SME Curriculum Integration in Schools","Include SME curriculum in schools",""],[2,"36","25","SME Curriculum Integration in Secondary Schools","Education Department to include SME curriculum in secondary schools","Education Department"]],"4":[[2,"41","4","Second National Financial Inclusion Strategy","Therefore, the 2nd NFIS 2016 - 2020 aims to have a clear road map and bring together initiatives from public sector, financial and non-financial institutions and other stakeholders such as donors to expand financial inclusion in PNG.",""],[2,"42","18","Financial Inclusion Expansion","Provision of financial products and services to reach an additional 2 million unbanked",""]],"5":[[2,"25","2","Fresh Fruits and Vegetables Supply Chain and Quality Improvement","Hence, the Government will support and invest in improving the supply value chain and improving the quality of fresh fruits and vegetables.",""],[2,"25","16","Sustainable Production and Best Farming Practices Promotion","Develop and promote adoption of sustainable production and best farming practices",""],[2,"25","18","Farmer Financial Services Access Initiative","Enable farmers to have access to financial services",""],[2,"25","19","Fruit and Vegetable Market Access and Marketing Support","Establish market access and improve marketing opportunities of fruits and vegetables farmers",""],[2,"25","24","Innovative Technologies, Processes and Information Systems Development and Adoption","Develop and adopt innovative technologies, processes and information systems",""]],"6":[[1,"11","1","Large-Scale Commercial Rice and Crop Development","the Government will invest significantly to grow rice on a large commercial scale to replace imports, grow our cocoa, oil palm, coffee, fresh produce, revitalise the livestock sector and promote the downstream processing of our raw materials.",""],[1,"15","5","Commercial Agriculture and Domestic Agro-Processing Promotion","Priority focus is on commercial agriculture to replace imports, increase exports and secure high value products by processing domestically.",""],[1,"38","3","Agricultural Commercialisation Support","especially in commercialisation of agricultural sector in which majority of our rural people are engaged",""],[1,"42","3","Manufacturing and Commercial Agriculture Growth Platform","Under the MTDP III, the intention is to make manufacturing, including downstream processing and import substitution, and commercial agriculture become the platform for national growth and development.",""],[1,"76","3","Agriculture and Agri-business Development","MTDP III focuses on promoting and expanding SME sector and developing agriculture and agri-business in the medium term.",""],[1,"81","2","Agriculture, Livestock, Fisheries, and Forestry Investment Expansion","The key investments will be in agriculture, livestock, fisheries, forestry, transport and infrastructure, small and medium enterprises, expansion of trade and other growth areas.",""],[2,"12","2","Plantation Rehabilitation and Export Volume Expansion","Given the potential that exists within the sector for improving quality and increasing quantity of agricultural produce, the focus of the sector in the medium term are to: (i) rehabilitate run-down plantations which should be prudently operated to boost export volumes;",""],[2,"12","2","Agricultural Sector Governance and Administration Reform","establish strong governance and administration system with clear policy guidelines to drive the sector forward;",""],[2,"12","2","Agricultural Biosecurity Strategy Development","develop a biosecurity strategy;",""],[2,"12","2","Agricultural Sector Partnership and Policy Support Framework","This will be achieved through establishing partnerships with the private sector, providing legislative and policy frameworks, establishing a central data centre to coordinate and track progress of the sector for future planning, and promote research and development for addressing food security issues and improving the quality and yield of food crops and major export commodities.",""],[2,"13","16","Agricultural Extension and Cooperative Society Support","Support extension services to farmers and Cooperative Societies to maintain quality value and supply chains",""],[2,"13","18","Farmer and MSME Finance and Market Access Support","Support farmers and MSMEs by giving them access to financial capital and identify viable domestic and international markets",""],[2,"13","20","Central Statistics Data Centre","Establish a central statistics data centre to coordinate and track progress of the sector for future planning purposes",""],[2,"13","22","Innovation and Technology Support for Industry Needs","Support learning, research and development in innovations and technology to cater for industry needs",""]],"7":[[2,"27","4","Illegal and Unregulated Fishing Control and Fisheries Market Expansion","Hence, the focus for the fisheries sector will be to increase exports and maximize economic returns through combating illegal and unregulated fishing within the EEZ, diversifying international market access, creating domestic markets for marine products and promoting SMEs in the fisheries sector among other priority activities.",""],[2,"27","4","Pacific Marine Industrial Zone Investment","These include investing in the Pacific Marine Industrial Zone (PMIZ) in Madang, investing in fisheries surveillance programs and building other marine infrastructure.",""],[2,"27","4","Fisheries Surveillance Programme Investment","These include investing in the Pacific Marine Industrial Zone (PMIZ) in Madang, investing in fisheries surveillance programs and building other marine infrastructure.",""],[2,"27","4","Marine Infrastructure Development","These include investing in the Pacific Marine Industrial Zone (PMIZ) in Madang, investing in fisheries surveillance programs and building other marine infrastructure.",""],[2,"28","17","NFA Monitoring, Control and Surveillance Capability Upgrade","Improve NFA MCS capability and increase coordination between relevant Government agencies to combat illegal, unreported and unregulated fishing within PNG's Exclusive Economic Zone (EEZ)",""],[2,"28","17","Interagency Coordination to Combat Illegal Fishing","increase coordination between relevant Government agencies to combat illegal, unreported and unregulated fishing within PNG's Exclusive Economic Zone (EEZ)",""],[2,"28","21","Marine Products Market Development Initiative","Create domestic and international market opportunities for marine products such as barramundi, crabs, lobsters etc.",""],[2,"28","23","SME and Local Participation Promotion in Fisheries","Promote the development of SMEs and local participation in the fisheries sector",""],[2,"28","25","Onshore Tuna Processing Requirement","Ensure all tuna caught in PNG waters is processed onshore",""],[2,"28","29","Fisheries Enabling Infrastructure Development","Development of key fisheries enabling infrastructure such as Wagang Fisheries Port, wharves, jetties, Fish markets, Cold storage & Ice plants.",""],[2,"28","31","Marine Resources Legislation Review","Review existing legislation and subordinate legislation for the conservation and sustainability of our marine resources.",""],[2,"28","33","Fisheries Extension Services Coordination with Provinces","Improve sector coordination with provinces to promote fisheries extension services to encourage community participation in fisheries development.",""],[2,"28","35","Onshore Tuna Processing Expansion","Increase onshore processing of tuna.",""],[2,"28","37","Sustainable Fisheries Management Practices","Promote sustainable fisheries management practices",""]],"8":[[1,"11","1","Forest Products Manufacturing and Round Log Export Ban","My Government will also promote manufacturing of more forest products and ban round log exports by 2020.",""],[1,"48","12","Sustainable Reforestation and Afforestation Programme","Encourage sustainable reforestation and afforestation programmes, and promote manufacturing of timber products.",""],[1,"48","12","Timber Products Manufacturing Promotion","Encourage sustainable reforestation and afforestation programmes, and promote manufacturing of timber products.",""],[2,"30","1","Round Log Export Ban","Hence, the Government aims to ban round logs exports by January 2021.",""],[2,"30","15","Forest Governance GIS Development","Develop a GIS for the purpose of planning and improved forest governance",""],[2,"30","17","National Reforestation Programme","Undertake reforestation in the country",""],[2,"30","18","Forest By-Products On-Shore Production Initiative","Decrease round log export and increase production of forest by-products on-shore",""],[2,"30","19","SME Development for Timber Products","Promote the development of SME's (timber products) in the sector",""],[2,"30","20","Forest Products Value-Addition and Export Promotion","Manufacture forest products as value adding products for the domestic market as well as for exports.",""],[2,"30","21","National Forest Resource Inventory System","Establish one (1) National Forest Resource Inventory System",""]],"9":[[2,"106","1","Climate Change Mitigation and Adaptation Strategy Implementation","Therefore, the focus for the country is to implement strategies of climate change and invest in activities that address climate change issues.",""],[2,"106","14","Climate Change Legislative and Regulatory Framework Improvement","Improved climate change legislative frameworks, policies, regulations and standards.",""],[2,"106","16","Climate Change Mitigation Funding and Support Negotiation","Negotiate to get improved funding, technical and institutional support for climate change mitigation in the country.",""],[2,"106","18","Sustainable Built Environment and Resilient Infrastructure Regulatory Framework","Develop policy and regulatory framework for the development of Sustainable Built Environment and Infrastructure - development of standards and regulations for climate proofed and resilient infrastructure.",""],[2,"106","20","Climate Change Education and Research and Development Support Programme","Support educational and research and development programmes associated with Climate Change management.",""],[2,"107","5","Climate-Proofing Regulation for Key Infrastructure","National regulation developed for climate proofing key infrastructure",""],[2,"107","10","National Vulnerability Assessment Training","Conduct National Vulnerability Assessment Training",""],[2,"107","11","Provincial Vulnerability Assessment Survey","Carry out Vulnerability assessment survey in the Provinces",""],[2,"107","12","Small Grant Programmes","Roll out Small grant programmes and Establish communication and early warning system",""],[2,"107","12","Communication and Early Warning System","Roll out Small grant programmes and Establish communication and early warning system",""],[2,"107","13","National REDD+ Finance Investment Plan Development","Development of a National REDD+ Finance Investment Plan",""],[2,"107","15","REDD+ Project Regulation Development","10. Develop a REDD+ Project Regulation",""]],"10":[[2,"105","24","Implementation of Multilateral Environmental Agreements","Implement Multilateral Environmental Agreements (MEAs) like the UNCCD, UNCBD and UNFCCC",""],[2,"105","25","MEA Obligations Implementation Coordination and Monitoring System","Coordinate the implementation of the MEAs' obligations & Establish monitoring systems to keep track of implementation progress",""]],"11":[[2,"31","3","National Tourism Master Plan Implementation","the National Tourism Master Plan (TMP) with its key result areas in Tourism Hub (Zone) Infrastructure Development, Tourism Brand Refreshment, Destination Marketing & Product Development, Capacity Building & Training, Coordination and Institutional Support (Provincial Tourism Bureaus), Eco-Tourism Development, Development & Establishment of the 3 new Tourism Markets, PNG online Marketing, and 2018 APEC related activities.",""],[2,"32","13","Tourism Safety Partnerships with Law and Justice Sector","Establish partnerships with the law and justice sector to create a safe environment for tourists",""],[2,"32","15","Affordable Tour and Business Package Provision","Provide affordable tour / business packages to encourage more business and bonafide tourists",""],[2,"32","16","Tourism Market Access Infrastructure Support","Provide enabling infrastructure for tourism market access",""],[2,"32","17","SME Promotion for Local Product Development","Promote SMEs in the sector to provide and improve PNG local products",""],[2,"32","18","Tourism Marketing Agents in Strategic International Locations","Tourism agents set up in strategic international locations to market PNG products",""],[2,"32","20","Local Market Infrastructure Construction","Proper market infrastructure constructed for locals to market their products",""]],"12":[[1,"10","3","Tuition Fee-Free Education","Province and District Service Improvement Program, Tuition Fee-Free education and Free Primary Health care program are currently addressing the development needs of our people.",""],[1,"14","12","Upgrade of National High Schools to Schools of Excellence","We will upscale our four National High Schools to Schools of Excellence as a deliberate quality of education improvement initiative.",""],[1,"14","12","Deployment of Specialist Secondary School Teachers","We will also bring in specialist Maths, Science and English teachers to assist us in improving our performance in these critical subjects in Secondary Schools.",""],[1,"14","12","Teacher Qualification Reform","We will also work towards policy reforms where all primary school teachers must have first degrees and all High School and Secondary School teachers must have Post Graduate Degree as minimum qualification;",""],[1,"53","14","Standard Based Education Reintroduction","Quality of education will be improved with re-introduction of Standard Based Education (SBE)",""],[1,"53","14","Teacher Recruitment and Training for Mathematics and Sciences","training and recruitments of more qualified teachers in Mathematics and Sciences including from overseas as an interim measure",""],[1,"53","14","Schools of Excellence Establishment","and establishment of Schools of Excellence",""],[1,"54","10","Quality Education Expansion and Access Improvement","The focus now in the medium term is to improve quality and continue to improve access and affordability.",""],[1,"54","10","Comprehensive Education Provision Across All Levels","During the next five years, the Government plans to provide quality education at all levels from basic elementary, primary and secondary education leading to TVET institutions, colleges and the universities.",""],[1,"59","4","National Education Curriculum STEM Enhancement","Improve the National Education Curriculum by focusing on STEM (Science, Technology, Engineering and Mathematics).",""],[1,"59","7","Teacher Qualification Standards Upgrade","Raise the minimum qualification standards for teachers from diploma to degree in primary and degree to higher level of qualification in secondary schools respectively.",""],[1,"59","8","Schools of Excellence Expansion","Increase the number of Schools of Excellence.",""],[1,"60","22","Establishment of Schools of Excellence","Establishment of Schools of Excellence",""],[2,"51","1","Tuition Fee Free Education Policy","The tuition Fee Free (TFF) Policy which address two of the three priorities has been the government's main policy focus to ensure accessibility and affordable education for all.",""],[2,"51","3","Education Quality Improvement Programme","the focus of the sector over the next five years is to improve the quality of education through providing adequate infrastructure, improve quality teaching and learning materials in mathematics and science, up-skill teachers through trainings, and most importantly roll out the Standard Based Education.",""],[2,"51","3","Schools of Excellence Re-establishment Initiative","the Government will promote and support the re-establishment of schools of excellence",""],[2,"51","3","Indian Mathematics and Science Teachers Program Partnership","also engage the Indian mathematics and science teachers program to promote quality teaching.",""],[2,"52","26","School Materials and Learning Resources Access Improvement","Improve and increase accesses of school materials and resources to enhance quality learning",""],[2,"52","30","Planning and Coordination Management Improvement","Improve planning and coordination management",""],[2,"52","32","Alternative Education Pathways Support","Promote and support alternative pathways in the education system such as FODE and TVET",""],[2,"53","1","Standard Base Curriculum Roll-out","Roll-out of standard base curriculum to all elementary, primary and secondary schools 20%",""],[2,"53","12","Secondary Schools Infrastructure Rehabilitation and Development Program","Secondary Schools Infrastructure Rehabilitation and Development Program",""]],"13":[[1,"11","4","Polytechnic Expansion for Youth Skills Development","To address high youth unemployment, my Government will focus on improving access to education and skills training by developing five more polytechnic institutions throughout the country.",""],[1,"44","11","TVET Expansion and Upgrading Programme","Reduce the import of technical skilled labour by upgrading and increasing the number TVET institutions.",""],[1,"59","5","TVET and FODE Access Improvement","Improve access to quality Technical Vocational Education and Training (TVET) and Flexible Open and Distance Education (FODE).",""],[1,"59","6","Improve Access to Higher Learning Institutions","Improve access to higher learning institutions.",""],[1,"60","24","Establishment of Five New Polytechnic Institutions","Five new Polytechnic Institutions are established by 2022",""],[2,"56","1","System Wide Vocational Reform Program","The Government has invested in the System Wide Vocational Reform program as a show of commitment to reform the sector.",""],[2,"56","1","Technical and Vocational Institution Capacity Building","Current focus is now on building the absorptive capacity of Technical, Vocational Education and Training institutions, Teachers and Nursing colleges and the Universities to address the bottle neck in the education system and the huge dropout rate.",""],[2,"56","3","TVET Skills Production Programme","The TVET sector will focus on producing more skilled practitioners in the medium term to meet the demand of the industries.",""],[2,"57","14","TVET Centre of Excellence Establishment","Improve TVET to be established as Centre of Excellence (COE)",""],[2,"57","16","PNG National Qualification Framework Promotion","Promote PNG National Qualification Framework (NQF)",""],[2,"57","18","TVET Infrastructure and Facilities Upgrade","Established or upgrade TVET infrastructures and facilities",""],[2,"57","20","Coordination Planning and Management Improvement","Improve coordination planning and management",""],[2,"57","28","Polytechnic Institutions Development Program","Polytechnic Institutions Development Program",""],[2,"57","29","Technical and Business College Rehabilitation Program","Technical and Business College Rehabilitation Program",""]],"14":[[2,"54","2","Tertiary Education Quality and Skills Development Programme","In the next five years, the government's focus through the sector is to provide quality tertiary education and skilled human resources that will respond to the manpower needs of the country.",""],[2,"55","15","Higher Education Endowment Fund","Improve higher education financing mechanisms - higher education endowment fund",""],[2,"55","17","Quality Assurance Measures Improvement and Application Expansion","Improve quality assurance measures and expand application",""],[2,"55","26","Turn-It-In Anti-Plagiarism System Roll-Out","Roll-out of Turn-It-In antiplagiarism system in the Universities",""]],"15":[[1,"11","4","Police, Army, and Justice Sector Expansion","My Government will increase the size of the police force, create a new army battalion in Hela Province and make further investments in correctional service, judiciary and other law enforcement agencies.",""],[1,"61","4","Law and Justice Sector Programme Rollout","Improve enforcement of the rule of law and prosecution by capacitating law and order agencies and further rollout of law and justice sector programs throughout most parts of the country including rural and remote areas.",""],[1,"61","7","Law and Justice Administration Improvement and Sector Program Rollout","During the next five years, the Government plans to improve law and justice administration and enforce rule of law and prosecution.",""],[1,"61","7","Capacity Building for Law and Order Agencies","Capacitating law and order agencies and further rollout of law and justice sector programs throughout most parts of the country including rural and remote areas is a priority of the Government.",""],[1,"62","17","Law and Justice Services Strengthening and Modernization","Strengthen, increase capacity and modernize the law and justice services at all levels.",""],[2,"78","2","Police Recruitment and Justice Infrastructure Improvement","However, with increasing population and the need for increased law and justice services in the country, more police personnel are recruited with due recruitment processes followed, improvement in the infrastructure, for instance, there are more than 400 gazetted court locations in the country but some had shut down due to lack of funding to maintain their facilities.",""],[2,"78","2","Prison Construction and Rehabilitation","The Court Orders for immediate construction and rehabilitation of certain prisons have also been a pressing issue in the aspects of development.",""],[2,"79","3","Police Recruitment Expansion","Increase recruitment of qualified policemen and policewomen",""],[2,"79","4","Reintroduction of Rural Lock-Ups","Reintroduce rural lock-ups in the 89 districts",""],[2,"79","6","Judicial Staffing Expansion","Increase the number of magistrates and judges to improve the backlog of court cases",""],[2,"79","12","Construction and Rehabilitation of Police Stations and Officers' Accommodations","Construction and rehabilitation of Police stations and officers accommodations",""],[2,"79","14","Construction of Rural Lock-Ups","Construction of rural lock-ups in the district",""],[2,"79","16","Construction and Rehabilitation of Court Facilities","Construction and rehabilitation of courts facilities",""],[2,"79","17","Magistrates Accommodation Construction","Construction of magistrates accommodation",""],[2,"79","18","Detainee Rehabilitation in Regional Prisons","Rehabilitation of detainees in 4 regional prisons",""]],"16":[[1,"12","2","MTDP III Implementation","I call on all partners and actors in development for your collective efforts to execute this important Plan.",""],[1,"17","3","National Planning Framework Coordination and M&E System","The PNG Planning and Responsibility Act 2016 defines the National Planning Framework for proper coordination of the national development strategy.",""],[1,"17","6","Medium- and Long-Term Development Planning, Implementation and Monitoring","Adopt a medium and long-term view to development planning, implementation and monitoring;",""],[1,"17","7","Medium-Term Development Plan Alignment with Vision 2050","Align all development plans over the medium term (2018-2022) towards achieving Vision 2050 targets;",""],[1,"20","11","Evidence-Based Planning Process Improvement","(viii) Improve evidence-based planning process.",""],[1,"24","13","Alignment of Sectoral, Provincial and District Plans","All sectoral, provincial and district plans must be aligned to implement Government's development priorities over the next five years.",""],[1,"26","2","MTDP III Monitoring and Evaluation Plan","Chapter 7 presents the Monitoring and Evaluation Plan.",""],[1,"26","2","MTDP III Risk Management Strategy","Chapter 8 discusses possible risks and sets out the risk management strategy for the implementation of the Plan.",""],[1,"33","7","National Planning and Monitoring and Evaluation Framework","The National Planning Framework and the Monitoring and Evaluation (M&E) Framework aims to improve coordination and implementation of the MTDP III in the next five years.",""],[1,"34","2","National Development Reporting and Monitoring Dialogue Mechanism","An effective and efficient ongoing dialogue between Department of National Planning and Monitoring (DNPM) and sectors and agencies at all levels is needed for an effective national reporting system to track and monitor and publish reports on the performance of the national development plans.","Department of National Planning and Monitoring (DNPM)"],[1,"34","3","Alignment of Sector and Sub-national Capital Investment Programs","Sectors and sub- national agencies are required to prioritise their capital investment programs in line with the government's development priority targets and goals to bring maximum returns to the economy.",""],[1,"83","6","Alignment of Sector Policies, Plans and Strategies to MTDP III Priorities","All sector policies, plans and strategies will be aligned to MTDP III priorities over the five-year implementation period to get the most from Government's limited resources.",""],[1,"84","1","Budget Alignment to MTDP III Priorities","all operational and development budgets need to be directed towards achieving the MTDP III KRAs and targets",""],[1,"85","1","MTDP III Delivery Monitoring and Evaluation Mechanism","DNPM will guide, monitor, and evaluate the delivery of MTDP III in an open and transparent manner; and communicate results to provide all stakeholders with accessible evidence-based information and data to ensure sustainable outcomes are achieved.",""],[1,"85","3","Monitoring, Evaluation and Reporting System","MTDP Ill's monitoring, evaluating and reporting system and processes enable the continuous generation of evidence to inform policy, national planning, program and project improvement, adaptation and management.",""],[1,"85","7","Evidence-Based Policy, Programme, and Project Management","Enable the evidence-based improvement, adaptation, and management of policies, programmes and projects;",""],[1,"85","8","Interdepartmental Collaboration and Cross-Learning Mechanism","Enable greater collaboration within and between departments and agencies to stimulate cross-learning and integration during implementation;",""],[1,"85","9","Evidence-Based Planning Data System","Build a system to collate and analyse data to inform future evidence-based planning and decision making;",""],[1,"85","10","MTDP III Budget Linkage Mechanism","Enable MTDP III plans and pipeline investments to be better linked to future budgets.",""],[1,"85","11","Medium-Term Development Plan Monitoring and Evaluation Guidance","MTDP M&E provides guidance on the M&E process for all State departments and agencies, sectors and organizations to collect and report on.",""],[1,"85","11","Sectoral Coordination and Information Management System","Secondly, it provides guidance on sectoral coordination and reporting, feedback, data sharing and information management system.",""],[1,"85","12","MTDP III Monitoring, Evaluation and Reporting System","It will enable the monitoring, evaluation and reporting of the MTDP III across sectors and organisations to become more consistent and systematic across policy areas, programmes and projects, and lead to more evidence-based programming, budgeting, and implementation.",""],[1,"85","12","National Data Centre and Database Systems","It will set the platform for the establishment of the national data centre/database systems that sectors and agencies can feed in to, compare progress from, and use for annual MTDP III planning, budgeting, and implementation.",""],[1,"86","1","Policy Monitoring and Reporting Framework","the MTDP III's performance, including the Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs), amongst others, is one of the policy areas for monitoring and reporting",""],[1,"87","2","Policy Monitoring and Evaluation Framework","Policy monitoring and evaluation - focuses on the Strategic Framework (Figure 7.2) and MTDP III Logical Framework (LogFrame) (details in Volume 2) that provide the implementation framework required to guide implementation, monitoring, evaluation and reporting across the contributing sectors.",""],[1,"87","3","Policy Monitoring and Evaluation Coordination Mechanism","The Policy M&E process should be coordinated and harmonised with all concerned sectors to ensure efficiency and effectiveness of the MTDP III intervention.",""],[1,"88","2","Policy Monitoring and Tracking System","Policy monitoring is concerned on tracking whether the MTDP III sectoral outputs are contributing to the national development outcomes and impacts; as well as the tracking activity implementation progress in delivering inputs and outputs.",""],[1,"88","3","Sector Performance Monitoring and Stakeholder Consultation Mechanism","It involves the continuous and timely collection of data, indicators and other relevant statistics and the sector performance reporting, analysis and validation with implementing institutions.",""],[1,"88","4","Policy Evaluation and Programme Assessment System","Policy evaluation provides an impartial and objective assessment on the MTDP III sectoral performance against the national development agenda, systematic assessment of the economic growth strategies and other focus areas, pinpoint institutional, coordination and policy issues, and promote greater learning within DNPM and executing agencies at all levels.",""],[1,"88","4","Big-Ticket Infrastructure Project Evaluation","It will also assess the effectiveness, relevance, efficiency, impact and sustainability of the Government's big-ticket infrastructure projects.",""],[1,"88","4","Annual, Mid-Term, and Final Evaluation Cycle","Annual, mid-term and final evaluation will be undertaken to make adjustment on changing circumstances and ensure that the MTDPIII goals and objectives are achieved as planned.",""],[1,"88","5","Annual MTDP III Results Monitoring and Review Framework","Annual reviews - will assess and validate achievements of the MTDP III outcomes and outputs planned for each year and the performance of growth strategies.",""],[1,"89","1","Mid-Term Evaluation of MTDP III","Mid-term evaluation - will provide mid-term analysis of the cumulative achievements against the MTDP Ill's goals and targets.",""],[1,"89","2","Independent Final Evaluation of MTDP III","Final evaluation - will be an independent evaluation to assess the overall achievements of the MTDP III during the implementation period, including the effectiveness, appropriateness and key results achieved by the key growth strategies, and document lessons learnt to be built on for the next MTDP.",""],[1,"89","11","MTDP III Monitoring, Evaluation and Reporting Support","The MTDP III M&E and reporting processes support the GoPNG's annual planning and budgeting cycle outlined in Table 7.2.",""],[1,"90","5","Annual Monitoring and Evaluation Planning Requirement","All State agencies must set goals or purpose for their annual M&E plan (to meet both internal and MTDP III information needs);",""],[1,"90","5","Monitoring and Evaluation Unit Establishment and Staffing","M&E unit established with designated technical and data management staff and budget for M&E and linked to Sector M&E working group.",""],[1,"90","15","MTDP III Monitoring and Evaluation System","Agencies should monitor MTDP III through: Quarter reviews/evaluations of the progress of the implementation of the PIP projects and MTDP III plans (see annexes for M&E templates) Capital Investment Project Report (CIPR) - Annex 2",""],[1,"91","2","Strategic Budget Committee Recommendation and Programme Performance Review","Recommendations to the Strategic Budget Committee; Intensive discussions with agencies; Funding suspension/termination of non-performing programmes or projects; Up scaling of promising projects; Building on the strengths of the planning and budgeting process; and",""],[1,"91","11","MTDP III Review and Evaluation Mechanism","Annual, mid-term and final (summative) review/evaluation of the MTDP III to inform the annual planning and budgeting process and build on the next MTDP formulation.",""],[1,"91","17","Evidence-Based Planning and Management System","Utilising evidence to enhance sector, agency, province, district, and project planning, budgeting, implementation, management and reporting (Adapting).",""],[1,"92","2","Quarterly Progress Reporting System","Departments, agencies and other public institutions will be required to submit quarterly reports to DNPM, which will be used to provide regular MTDP III progress reports to the Central Agencies Coordinating Committee (CACC) and the National Executive Council (NEC) (see Annexes 2, 3 &4).","DNPM | Central Agencies Coordinating Committee (CACC) | National Executive Council (NEC)"],[1,"92","3","MTDP III Reporting, Analysis, Validation, and Dissemination Mechanism","Overall MTDP III reporting, analysis, validation, and dissemination will be managed by the DNPM technical secretariat, which will monitor and report on national headline indicators using data from delivery departments, agencies and institutions, including for example the National Statistics Office, through the PNG Strategy for Development of Statistics (PNGSDS), sector reviews, and independent evaluations.","DNPM technical secretariat | National Statistics Office"],[1,"95","10","Strengthening of the National Reporting System","DNPM shall ensure that national reporting system is strengthened, and relevant reports are produced and published on a regular basis on the MTDP outcomes and the annual budgets.","DNPM"],[1,"95","10","Implementation of the MTDP Monitoring and Evaluation Plan","Further, it shall ensure that relevant State agencies and other stakeholders will contribute to the implementation of the MTDP M&E plan, promote joint M&E undertakings and data sharing.","DNPM"],[1,"96","1","Agency and Sector Plan Performance Management and M&E Strengthening","Central departments and sector agencies play a major role in the monitoring, evaluation and reporting of the MTDP III, especially in relation to the agency/sector plan performance management, M&E coordination and facilitation role.",""],[1,"96","2","Monitoring and Evaluation Information Use for Policy and Budget Decisions","They should use the M&E information to make decisions about agency/sector policies, programmes and projects; inform annual budget decisions; produce sector performance reports and statistics; and ensure tracking of progress in the achievements of the UN's SDGs.",""],[1,"97","3","MTDP III Monitoring and Evaluation System","DNPM, in collaboration with all concerned agencies and organisations at all levels, must ensure the use of data and information generated from M&E through the following:","DNPM"],[1,"101","4","Implementation Progress Monitoring of Government Development Plans and Programmes","ii. improve understanding on the implementation progress of the Government's development plans and programmes; and",""]],"17":[[1,"64","14","Agency Capacity Strengthening","Improve the capacity of agencies to respond to needs and development challenges.",""],[1,"64","16","Public Service Regulations Enforcement","Enforce the relevant Public Service regulations",""],[1,"64","17","Public Institution Monitoring and Evaluation Mechanisms","Develop monitoring and evaluation mechanisms to ensure public institutions become accountable",""],[1,"67","11","Monitoring, Evaluation, Accountability and Transparency Strengthening Initiative","Strengthen and enforce monitoring and evaluation, accountability and transparency initiatives.",""],[1,"67","13","Public Sector Reform Strengthening","Improve and strengthen public sector reform in the institutional structures and human resource capacity, procurement and service delivery mechanism.",""],[1,"67","14","Independent Commission Against Corruption Establishment Legislation","Legislate to establish the Independent Commission Against Corruption.",""],[1,"68","6","Anti-Corruption Initiatives Support","Support Anti- Corruption initiatives",""],[1,"83","1","Private Sector Governance Strengthening","The Government is investing in key enablers and as a growth facilitator; allow an increasingly vigorous private sector to develop; and strengthen governance in interactions with the private sector.",""]],"18":[[1,"25","14","National Service Delivery Framework","The PNG Planning and Monitoring Responsibility Act 2016 establishes the National Service Delivery Framework (NSDF) for guiding the delivery of services throughout the country.",""],[2,"110","2","Services Improvement Program Capacity Support","the National Government has continued to resource the capacity of all the provinces and districts through the Services Improvement Program (SIP).",""],[2,"110","3","District Development Authorities Service Improvement Programs","With the full operationalisation of the District Development Authorities (DDAs), service delivery targets will be reasonably resourced and delivered under the Service Improvement Programs (SIPs).",""],[2,"110","3","Subnational Alignment with MTDP Priorities and National Service Delivery Framework","Hence, it is important that subnational governments clearly articulate their strategies, policies and plans in line with the MTDP priorities, provide active leadership in implementing and monitoring the national policies at the subnational level.",""],[2,"110","11","Whole-of-Government Service Delivery Approach","Adopt a whole-of government approach in service delivery.",""],[2,"110","15","DDA Capacity Building for Effective Service Delivery","Build capacity for effective service delivery through the DDA's.",""],[2,"110","18","Private Sector and Community Stakeholder Partnership Strengthening","Strengthen partnerships with the private sector and community-based stakeholders to address service development.",""],[2,"110","21","PFMA Enforcement in Provinces and Districts","Enforce the Public Finance Management Act (PFMA) in provinces and districts",""]],"19":[[2,"88","12","Foreign Policy Finalization and Implementation","Finalize new Foreign Policy and implement to enhance PNG's international standing for national interests",""],[2,"88","16","Regional and International Partnership Strengthening for Trade and Economic Relations","Strengthening key partnerships through PIF and other Regional Organizations and others such as ASEAN, ACP-EU, the Commonwealth, NAM, APEC and regional/international agreements to strengthen trade and economic relations",""],[2,"90","23","Establishment of Regional Offices","Establish regional offices in Brussels, Singapore, Suva, Guangzhou",""]],"20":[[1,"14","3","Election System Overhaul and Reform","Total overhaul and reform is required for the next election;",""],[1,"15","2","Electronic Voting System Replacement","To replace the current manual voting system with electronic one and returning to the first-past-the-post voting system by the 2022 National Elections;",""],[1,"59","22","Electoral System Reform to Increase Women's Political Participation","Review and reform current electoral systems to encourage women's participation in political decision-making.",""],[1,"67","15","Electoral Processes and Systems Strengthening","Strengthen electoral processes and systems.",""],[1,"68","5","Electronic Voting System for the National Election","Conduct the National Election in 2022 with the Electronic Voting System",""]],"21":[[1,"59","23","Women in Leadership and Decision-Making Targets and Measures","Establish targets and measures to increase the number of women in leadership/management and decision-making.",""],[1,"59","24","Women's Political and Economic Empowerment Advocacy Programme","Work in partnership with other stakeholders through advocacy programmes promoting women's political and economic empowerment.",""],[1,"60","8","Ethical and Cultural Safety Nets for Vulnerable Groups","Strengthen ethical and cultural safety nets to protect and provide the rights to services and communal engagement for vulnerable segment of society.",""],[1,"74","9","Girls' Education and Employment Promotion","3. Promote education and employment opportunities for girls.",""],[1,"84","4","Corporate Community Obligation Framework","Companies, especially in resource sector must take a greater responsibility for community obligation for people directly affected by their operation whilst the Government will take responsibilities for others.",""],[2,"95","14","Girls' Education and Employment Promotion","Promote education and employment opportunities for girls.",""],[2,"98","4","Gender-Based Programs and Initiatives","The focus for the medium term is to support and implement gender based programs and initiatives to improve the indicators for gender.",""],[2,"99","25","Women's Economic Empowerment and Rights Awareness Initiative","Increase women's access to economic opportunities and awareness of their economic rights.",""],[2,"99","26","Strengthen Family Welfare and Women and Child Protection Legislation","Prevent and eliminate violence against women and children by strengthening legislation on family welfare, child and women protection",""],[2,"99","28","Anti-Discrimination Legislation Strengthening","Strengthen legislation to safeguard people from being stigmatised due to race, cultural and religious orientation.",""],[2,"99","29","Women's Political Participation Promotion","Promote women's political participation at all levels of government.",""],[2,"99","31","Women Entrepreneurs Skills Development and Capacity Enhancement Programme","Implement the entrepreneur skills development training and capacity enhancement programs for women (training courses conducted)",""],[2,"102","2","Community-Oriented Livelihood Empowerment Approaches","community oriented approaches are required to empower and improve community livelihoods.",""],[2,"102","2","Accessibility and Disability Inclusion Measures","initiatives such as sign language interpreters during news broadcasts, buildings with wheelchair access ramps and restrooms for people living with disability indicate continued support for this sector.",""],[2,"102","2","Social Protection Strategy for VDG Economic Participation","Social protection strategies are also required to boost VDG participation within the economy and is emphasized in PNG's National Policy on Social Protection 2015-2020.",""],[2,"103","12","Policy and Legislation Review for Vulnerable Citizens","Review policy and legislation to cater for the specific needs of the vulnerable citizens",""],[2,"103","14","Infrastructure and Utilities Improvement for Vulnerable Citizens","Improve infrastructure and utilities to service the needs of the vulnerable citizens",""],[2,"103","16","Human Rights Education and Awareness Campaign","Promote education and awareness on basic human rights.",""],[2,"103","18","Community-Based Partnership for Inclusivity","Strengthen partnership with community-based organisations and donors to progress the principle of inclusivity in national and community life.",""],[2,"103","20","Ethical and Cultural Safety Nets for Vulnerable Groups","Strengthen ethical and cultural safety nets to protect and provide for the rights to services and communal engagement for vulnerable segment of society.",""],[2,"103","22","Community Learning and Development Centres","Establish Community Learning and Development Centres",""],[2,"103","23","Rehabilitation, Care and Protection Programs","Develop and maintain appropriate rehabilitation, care and protection programs",""],[2,"103","24","Rehabilitation Centre Reclamation and Refurbishment","Rehabilitation centres for people living with disability reclaimed and refurbished",""],[2,"103","25","Government-Private MOUs for Education and Awareness","Establish MOUs between government and private organisations for education and awareness purposes",""]],"22":[[1,"55","3","Sports Stadium Upgrading Programme","The Government plans to upgrade Sports Stadiums in Lae and Goroka to international standard",""],[1,"55","3","Sports Personnel Training and Incentive Programme","train more skilled personnel by facilitating exposure to quality training programs in-country and abroad and incentivise sports personnel to aspire to excel in the medium term",""],[1,"59","18","Professional Sports Person Support Programme","Promote and support professional sports persons in sporting codes.",""],[1,"59","19","Sports Facilities Upgrade and International Standards Programme","Build and upgrade sporting facilities to international standards to encourage international sporting events and promote sports tourism.",""],[1,"59","20","Compulsory Sports and Physical Education in Schools and Tertiary Institutions","Ensure that sports and physical education is taught as a compulsory subject in schools and tertiary institutions.",""],[2,"60","1","Sports Facilities Infrastructure Development","The sector has undergone infrastructure development of sports facilities with upgrading of current outdoor facilities and construction of additional two stadiums.",""],[2,"60","2","Sports Facilities Development and Stadium Redevelopment Programme","The sector will focus on the development of sporting facilities for community, national and international sporting events, integrating sport in schools and supporting the coordination and development of domestic sporting competitions from grassroots to elite levels.",""],[2,"60","2","Lae and Goroka Stadium Redevelopment","The Government over the next five years will focus on redeveloping the Lae and Goroka Stadiums among other priorities of the sector.",""],[2,"61","2","Sports Facilities Revenue Generation and Program Subsidy Mechanism","Generate income to upkeep and maintain the sports facilities and subsidize sports programs.",""],[2,"61","4","Construction of New International Sports Facilities","Construct new international sports facilities in PNGSF institutions and provinces in partnership with Provincial Governments and other key stakeholders.",""],[2,"61","6","Sports Federation and Community Resource Support Initiative","Empower National Sports Federations, Educational Institutions and Communities through resource support and allow accessibility to sports facilities.",""],[2,"61","8","Coach and Sports Administrator Upskilling and Athlete Services Expansion","Upskill more coaches and sports administrators and increase services to athletes.",""],[2,"61","10","PNG Grassroots Games Mass Participation Initiative","Increase mass participation in PNG Grassroots Games.",""],[2,"61","12","Sports Excellence Programs Rollout","Roll out sports excellence programs throughout PNG using regional sports facilities.",""],[2,"61","14","School Sports and Physical Education Programme","Develop sports programs or physical education in schools",""],[2,"61","18","Inter-School Carnivals Promotion","Encourage and promote inter-school carnivals",""]],"23":[[1,"11","6","APEC Summit Investment Promotion Initiative","We intend to use the opportunity of hosting the 2018 Asia Pacific Economic Cooperation (APEC) Summit to secure high impact projects, which are necessary to building our economic growth base.",""],[1,"11","6","National Trade and Investment Promotion Campaign","Collectively, we need to aggressively market trade and investment opportunities in our country to attract more foreign direct investments.",""],[1,"17","2","Export Expansion Strategy","Under the MTDP III, the Government will focus on: (2) increasing exports,",""],[1,"32","3","National Trade Policy Framework","The National Trade Policy provides a policy framework to promote sustainable economic growth for Papua New Guinea through key investments directed at the renewable sector, encouraging downstream processing of raw materials, import substitution and export diversification.",""],[1,"32","3","Competitive Export Base Development","It also creates an environment to build a competitive and sustainable export base to stimulate economic growth.",""],[1,"32","3","Trade Agreements and Market Access Framework","The Policy also sets the framework for trade agreements and trade negotiations by identifying the sectors with comparative advantage, and opening up market access for exports.",""],[1,"39","4","National Trade Policy Framework","The National Trade Policy provides a policy framework to promote sustainable economic growth for Papua New Guinea through key investments directed at the renewable sector, encouraging downstream processing of raw materials, import substitution and export diversification.",""],[1,"44","8","Export Expansion for Major Commodity Sectors","1.2 Increase exports of major agricultural commodities, fisheries products, processed timber, manufacturing, and minerals.",""],[1,"45","7","Export Base Expansion Initiative","The government's expansion of the export base will promote exports of domestically manufactured and produced commodities and goods.",""],[1,"47","1","Foreign Direct Investment Incentive and Attraction Measures","In the medium term, the Government plans to provide incentives and conducive environment to attract more FDIs.",""],[2,"39","2","National Trade Policy Framework","The National Trade Policy provides a policy framework for trade agreements and trade negotiations, for the identification of sectors with comparative advantage, and for opening up market access in sectors that can have an impact on the economy and create jobs.",""],[2,"39","3","National Trade Office Establishment","one of the major immediate tasks is to establish a National Trade Office that will implement the National Trade Policy.",""],[2,"40","2","Transparent and Predictable Policy and Regulatory Environment","Promote a transparent and predictable policy and regulatory environment",""],[2,"40","4","Trade-Related Infrastructure and Services Development","Develop trade related infrastructure and services",""],[2,"40","8","Sector-Specific Trade Policy Development","Develop sector specific policies for trade",""],[2,"40","12","Import and Export Cost Reduction Measures","Implement measures for reducing import and export costs",""],[2,"40","20","Trade Institutions Capacity and Efficiency Strengthening","Strengthen the capacity and efficiency of trade institutions",""],[2,"40","23","Trade Remedies Legislation","2. Enact trade remedies legislation",""],[2,"40","26","WTO Trade Facilitation Agreement Compliance","5. Achieve full compliance with the WTO Trade Facilitation Agreement",""]],"24":[[1,"12","1","Population Growth Reduction and Stabilization Measure","Together, we must all take responsibility to reduce the growth rate and maintain the population at a more sustainable level that we can manage as other countries have done successfully.",""],[1,"20","10","Population Growth Management and Family Planning Promotion","Manage population growth at a sustainable level and promote family planning;",""],[1,"36","5","National Population Policy 2015-2024","To address this concern, the National Population Policy 2015-2024 was developed to give emphasis on managing population as a key development priority with population as the centre of development.",""],[1,"73","8","Population Growth Management and Economic Balance Policy","Population growth would have to be managed so that the growing needs of a country are adequately met by its economic performance.",""],[1,"74","7","National Population Policy Implementation","Adopt and implement the National Population Policy by promoting development initiatives that are human centric, balance and sustainable.",""],[1,"74","8","Population Education Curriculum Integration","Integrate Population Education into the curriculum of teachers' college, secondary and primary education.",""],[1,"74","10","Reproductive Health Education and Care Partnerships","Government to strengthen partnerships with Private sectors and NGOs to provide reproductive health education and health care",""],[1,"74","11","Population Awareness and Promotion Programmes","Provinces and Districts to take ownership of population agenda by coming up with comprehensive promotional and awareness programmes under partnership arrangements with churches and other non-government organisations.",""],[1,"74","12","Fertility Reduction Incentive Measures","To manage population growth by controlling fertility rate through the provision of incentives such as taxation and targeted education scholarships.",""],[1,"74","16","Reproductive Health Care and Family Planning Initiatives","Intensify the implementation of the Reproductive Health Care and Family Planning initiatives",""],[2,"94","2","Population Development Partnership and Implementation Program","Partnerships with all levels of government departments and agencies especially, NGOs, CSOs and Private Sector are critical for effective implementation programs that target population.",""],[2,"94","3","Population Awareness and Reproductive Health and Education Programs","the focus for the medium term will be on promoting and supporting population awareness and investing in reproductive health and education programs.",""],[2,"95","10","National Population Policy Implementation","Adopt and implement the National Population Policy by promoting development initiatives that is human centric and within a paradigm of balance and sustainability",""],[2,"95","12","Integration of the National Population Policy into Sector, District and Provincial Plans","Integration of the National Population Policy into Sector, Districts and Provincial Plans to operationalize the National Population Policy",""],[2,"95","16","Reproductive Health Education and Health Care Partnership Programme","Government to strengthen partnerships with Private sectors and NGO's to provide reproductive health education and health care",""],[2,"95","18","Population Awareness and Advocacy Programmes","Provinces and districts to take ownership of population agenda by coming up with comprehensive promotional and awareness programmes and supporting Churches and CSOs.",""],[2,"95","19","Controlled Fertility Incentives and Education Scholarship Programme","To manage population growth through controlled fertility rate through the provision of incentives such as taxation and targeted education scholarship.",""],[2,"95","21","Population Management Awareness Programs","Coverage of population management awareness programs throughout educational institutions and communities",""],[2,"95","22","Reproductive Health Awareness and Comprehensive Family Planning Services","Coverage of programs with awareness on reproductive health and care such as comprehensive family planning services",""]],"25":[[1,"26","2","MTDP III Marketing and Communication Strategy","Finally, Chapter 9 - the marketing and communication strategy - explains how the information on MTDP III will be communicated to the various stakeholders and to draw more feedback during the implementation period of this Plan.",""],[1,"59","16","Youth Civic Engagement and Enrichment Support","Support youths in civic engagements and other schools, communities and society based enrichment activities.",""]],"26":[[2,"63","4","National Transport Strategy and Medium Term Transport Plan Implementation","The Medium Term Transport Plan (MTTP) 2014-2018 was formulated as the vessel through which the challenges and issues are addressed through identification and prioritization of projects.",""],[2,"63","4","Transport Infrastructure Investment and Maintenance Programme","MTDP III will continue to invest in vital transport infrastructure, especially the maintenance of the existing National Road Network (NRN), economically vital missing link roads, major sea ports and airports.",""],[2,"64","2","National Road Network Rehabilitation and Upgrade Programme","Hence, the Government will continue to invest in the rehabilitation, maintenance, reconstruction and upgrading programs on the existing National Road Network, construction of economically vital missing link roads; and design, reconstruction and upgrading of aging and obsolete bridges.",""],[2,"64","2","Missing Link Road Construction Programme","Hence, the Government will continue to invest in the rehabilitation, maintenance, reconstruction and upgrading programs on the existing National Road Network, construction of economically vital missing link roads; and design, reconstruction and upgrading of aging and obsolete bridges.",""],[2,"64","2","Aging Bridge Reconstruction and Upgrading Programme","Hence, the Government will continue to invest in the rehabilitation, maintenance, reconstruction and upgrading programs on the existing National Road Network, construction of economically vital missing link roads; and design, reconstruction and upgrading of aging and obsolete bridges.",""],[2,"65","2","National Road Network Rehabilitation and Maintenance","Rehabilitate and maintain all National Road Network (NRN) including bridges",""],[2,"65","4","Transport Maintenance Financing Mechanism","Establish fund sources for maintenance.",""],[2,"65","6","Independent Road Inspection and Quality Assurance Entity","Establish an independent Road Inspection (Quality Assurance/Audit) Entity for road design and materials quality inspection; and for the verification and approval of standard unit costs for all types of road works",""],[2,"65","14","Institutional Functional Reviews for Service Delivery Improvement","Institutional Functional Reviews between DoW, NRA & IDA to improve Performance, Governance and Accountability for better use of scares resources for effective delivery of services.","DoW | NRA | IDA"],[2,"65","17","Road Maintenance User-Pay System","Effective road maintenance user-pay system established",""],[2,"65","24","Highlands Highway Rehabilitation Program","Highlands Highway Rehabilitation Program",""],[2,"65","27","Coastal District Road and Rehabilitation Program","Coastal District Road and Rehabilitation Program(DRRP)",""]],"27":[[2,"66","3","Maritime Sector Reform Programme","The four key programmes that will be implemented over the next five years are: (i) reforming the maritime sector;",""],[2,"66","3","Major Port Rehabilitation and Upgrade Programme","The four key programmes that will be implemented over the next five years are: (ii) rehabilitate and upgrade major ports and its related facilities;",""],[2,"66","3","Strategic Small Wharves and Jetties Rehabilitation Programme","The four key programmes that will be implemented over the next five years are: (iii) rehabilitate and upgrade important strategic small wharves and jetties;",""],[2,"66","3","Maritime Transport Safety and Security Improvement Programme","The four key programmes that will be implemented over the next five years are: (iv) improve safety and security on maritime transport systems.",""],[2,"67","2","Major Ports Rehabilitation and Upgrade","Rehabilitate and upgrade major ports and its related facilities",""],[2,"67","4","Navigation and Monitoring Equipment Rehabilitation and Upgrade","Rehabilitate, upgrade and install international standard navigational & monitoring equipment",""],[2,"67","5","Strategic Jetties and Wharves Construction and Upgrade","Construct and upgrade of strategic jetties and wharves",""],[2,"67","7","Maritime Transport Services Improvement","Promote Maritime Transport Services that enhances Affordable, Safe and Secure water travel services.",""],[2,"67","10","Wharf and Jetty Rehabilitation","3. Rehabilitate wharves and jetties",""]],"28":[[2,"68","3","Rural Air Transport Connectivity and Airport Upgrade Programme","The Government in the medium term will focus on linking majority of the rural hinterlands, especially the economically vibrant isolated market segments of the country through the provision of a safe, reliable and cost-effective air transport service that promotes international tourism and greater socio-economic activities.",""],[2,"68","3","Major Airport Upgrade, Rehabilitation and Extension","There will be continued investment for upgrade, rehabilitation and extension of all major airports for higher capacity aircrafts under the new CADIP.",""],[2,"68","3","Rural Airstrip Rehabilitation and Access Expansion Programme","There will also be investment in rehabilitation and opening access to rural areas through the rural airstrips programs implemented by the Rural Airstrip Agency (RAA).",""],[2,"69","7","Air Navigational Aid Systems Improvement","Improvement in air navigational aid systems for major airports",""],[2,"69","12","Aviation Market Competition Promotion","Promote competition in both domestic and international aviation markets that enhance affordable air travel services for citizens, tourists and cargo.",""],[2,"69","14","Major Airport Upgrade, Rehabilitation and Expansion Programme","Upgrade, rehabilitate and extend all major airports to cater for bigger aircrafts",""],[2,"69","16","Airport Safety and Security Upgrade Programme","Upgrade airports to international safety and security standards, including CASA certifications",""],[2,"69","18","Rural Airstrip Rehabilitation and Upgrading","Rehabilitate, open and make more rural airstrips usable",""],[2,"69","25","National Airport Upgrading and Development Program","National Airport Upgrading and Development Program",""]],"29":[[1,"11","4","National Broadband Fibre Optic Cable Project","One of the most important projects is the Kumul Submarine Fibre Optic Cable across the Coral Sea and the domestic cable from Port Moresby to Wutung, West Sepik to enable the high-speed Internet connection and reduce the cost of internet and other services.",""],[1,"50","3","Submarine Cable and National Network Expansion","Information and communication technology (ICT) is expected to improve dramatically with the submarine cable between Sydney and Port Moresby and expansion of network throughout the nation.",""],[1,"51","8","Submarine Cable and National Fibre Optic Network Deployment","Establish submarine cable between Papua New Guinea and Australia with installation of fibre optic network throughout the country to provide affordable, high-speed internet access to communities.",""],[2,"70","10","IGIS Network and National Data Centre Provincial Connectivity","Connect 22 provinces onto the IGIS network and National Data Centre",""],[2,"70","17","Regulatory and Compliance Standards Enforcement","Establish and enforce stringent regulatory and compliance standards and procedures",""],[2,"70","18","Mobile Phone Market Liberalization","Liberalize the mobile phone market",""],[2,"70","19","Fibre Optic National Transmission Network Completion","Complete fibre optic NTN program connecting it to the international gateway",""],[2,"70","20","National Communications Infrastructure Strengthening","Strengthen the national communications infrastructure",""],[2,"70","21","Rural ICT Roll-Out Programs","Support Rural ICT Roll-Out Programs",""],[2,"70","22","IGIS Integration of Government Agencies","Complete the IGIS integration of all the government agencies",""],[2,"71","1","Fibre Optic NTN International Gateway Connection","Connect the fibre optic NTN to the international gateway",""],[2,"71","2","National Communication Infrastructure Strengthening and Support","Fully strengthen and support national communication infrastructure",""],[2,"71","8","IGIS Roll Out Programme for Digital TV and Radio Signal Transmission","IGIS Roll out Programme - Government Coverage Capacity - Digital TV and Radio Signal Transmission",""]],"30":[[1,"11","5","District Town Water Supply Systems Program","The MTDP III will focus on the following district programs: district hospitals, district offices, district town water supply systems, district town roads upgrading and sealing, and rural electrification program.",""],[1,"70","1","National WaSH Authority Establishment","National Water, Sanitation and Hygiene (WaSH) Authority will be established with aim of overseeing the implementation of the WaSH Policy.",""],[1,"72","8","National Water, Sanitation and Hygiene Authority","Establish National Water, Sanitation and Hygiene Authority to oversee and coordinate the water, sanitation and hygiene services.",""],[1,"72","9","Water, Sanitation and Hygiene Program","Water, Sanitation and Hygiene program to provide safe water and improved sanitation services to all rural households and business houses.",""],[1,"72","10","Urban Safe Water and Sanitation Service Provision","Water PNG Limited to provide safe water and improved sanitation services for all urban households and business houses.",""],[1,"72","11","Safe Water and Sanitation Services for Health and Education Institutions","Water PNG Limited to provide safe water and improved sanitation services to all health and education institutions in the country.",""],[1,"72","28","Port Moresby Sewerage System Improvement Project","9. Port Moresby Sewerage System Improvement Project",""],[1,"72","31","Goroka Town Sewerage System Upgrade","Upgrade Goroka Town Sewerage System",""],[1,"72","33","District Town Water Supply System Completion","Complete the water supply system in all District Towns",""],[1,"73","2","Completion of Provincial Town Water Supply Systems","Complete Provincial Town Water Supply Systems in all Provincial Towns (Mendi, Kerema, Daru, Vanimo, Kurumul, Tari, etc.)",""]],"31":[[2,"13","13","Downstream Processing Policy and Legislative Frameworks","Provide legislative and policy frameworks that encourage shift towards more downstream processing",""],[2,"13","36","Special Economic Zone Development","Development of Special Economic Zone (Sepik, Sandaun, Kikori, West Coast Manus, Baiyer Valley, Ramu Valley)",""],[2,"14","1","Palm Oil Downstream Processing Expansion","Hence, the industry aims to move into milling and other downstream processing ventures.",""],[2,"14","1","Palm Oil Industry Regulation","The regulation of the industry is vital in ensuring that local farmers who make up the primary supply and value chain move into milling and other downstream processing activities.",""],[2,"14","11","Oil Palm Industry Corporation Act Review and Capacity Strengthening","Review and amend the current Oil Palm Industry Corporation Act, 1992 and strengthen OPIC's capacity",""],[2,"15","17","Productive Public-Private Partnership Promotion","Promote productive public private partnership for extension, research and industry operations",""]],"32":[[1,"46","4","National Land Development Programme","There were several programmes being pursued, including the National Land Development Programme, which resulted in key reforms in enabling legislations and customary land ownership.",""],[1,"46","4","Formal Land Market Expansion","MTDP III will pursue to make more land available in the formal market for the land-owners to become effective partners and benefit from its development.",""],[2,"37","2","National Land Development Program","The National Land Development Program launched in 2007 focused on addressing issues affecting; Land Administration, Land Dispute Settlement and Customary Land Development.",""],[2,"38","13","ILG and Customary Land Registration Expansion","Increase number of ILGs registrations and Customary Land registration (VLCR)",""],[2,"38","14","Land Dispute Resolution through Mediation and Land Courts","Effective Land Dispute Resolutions through Mediation and Land Courts.",""],[2,"38","15","Alienated Land Development for Sustainable Urban and Rural Development","Alienated Land Development - more Alienated land being used for sustainable urban and rural developments in provinces and priority economic corridors.",""],[2,"38","16","National Sustainable Land Use Policy and Legislation Review","National Sustainable Land Use Policy & Legislation Review to upgrade physical planning functions and Land Use Information Management System is established to clearly identify general statues to all land and managing information of Land Use activities in PNG including all stakeholders land uses and integrate DLPP's Land Information Management System.",""],[2,"38","17","Development Planning and Land Use Audit","Develop development plans and do overall land use Audit to take stock of both Alienated & customary land",""],[2,"38","18","Land Legislation and Regulatory Update","Update all outdated Land Legislations and related regulations and policies with all relevant stakeholders",""],[2,"38","19","Automated Land Information System","DLPP's Automated Land Information System is in operation",""],[2,"38","20","LeAP Project Re-initiation and Go-Live","Re-initiation of LeAP Project and \"Go Live\"",""],[2,"38","21","System Link Program for DLPP Regional Offices","Begin System Link program for DLPP regional offices and relevant stakeholders",""],[2,"38","22","DLPP Roll-out Program","Begin Roll- out program within DLPP HQ, Regional sites and relevant stakeholders",""],[2,"38","23","DLPP System Maintenance and Support","Completion of the implementation Phase whilst continuous support maintenance of the system towards DLPP HQ, Regional sites and relevant stakeholders",""],[2,"38","24","Increase Registration of Incorporated Land Groups and Bankable Customary Land Leases","Double the registration of ILGs and Bankable Customary Land Leases",""],[2,"38","25","ILG and Customary Land Registration Programme","Encourage and implement the registration of ILGs & Customary land with a minimum of200 ILGs and 50 customary leases",""]],"33":[[1,"11","2","Large Resource Projects Delivery","My Government is working hard to deliver large resource projects like the second PNG LNG Project, Wafi-Golpu Mine and other projects.",""],[1,"48","14","Mining and Petroleum Project Development with Tax Agreement Revision","Explore and develop new mines (Wafi-Golpu and Frieda River Copper Mine) and petroleum and LNG projects with revision of tax agreements.",""]],"34":[[2,"33","2","Policy and Legislative Frameworks for Trade and Investment Support","There is need for policy and legislative frameworks to support export and imports and investments in the country",""],[2,"33","2","Local Content Requirements for FDI Programs","establishment of proper national content in the FDI Programs to bring maximum benefits to the country",""],[2,"33","2","FDI Tax Incentive Structuring","FDI promotion incentives of tax exemptions and holidays to be structured to benefit PNG during the term of the project",""],[2,"33","2","Domestic Production and Industry Competitiveness Support","and domestic production and industries to meet competition of imported goods and also volume of quality to meet the market demand",""],[2,"33","3","Industrial Parks Development Programme","The Government will focus on developing key infrastructure such as the development of industrial parks in Port Moresby, Kundiawa and Lae among other priorities.",""],[2,"34","12","Legal and Regulatory Framework for Manufacturing Sector Reform","Create a legal and regulatory framework to provide the roadmap and guide the structural reforms and policy direction needed to create a vibrant and active manufacturing sector.",""],[2,"34","15","Export Standards Compliance Support","Increase exports by ensuring that nationally manufactured products comply with international standards.",""],[2,"34","17","Foreign Direct Investment Promotion","Promote Foreign Direct Investment into the sector.",""],[2,"34","18","Export and Import Substitution Manufacturing Hubs in Free Trade and Industrial Zones","Promote export & import substitution manufacturing hubs in Free Trade and Industrial zones throughout PNG",""],[2,"34","19","Manufacturing Policy for Inclusive Growth","Formulate policy on manufacturing that promotes the inclusive growth agenda.",""],[2,"34","20","National Content Plans for Major Investments","Formulate National Content Plans associated with major investments aimed at growing the domestic manufacturing industry and SME.",""],[2,"34","21","SME Participation in Manufacturing Expansion","Increased participation of SMEs into manufacturing of food and beverages, textiles and clothing, arts and crafts and other building and construction products.",""]],"35":[[1,"10","3","Free Primary Health Care Program","Province and District Service Improvement Program, Tuition Fee-Free education and Free Primary Health care program are currently addressing the development needs of our people.",""],[1,"11","5","District Hospitals Program","The MTDP III will focus on the following district programs: district hospitals, district offices, district town water supply systems, district town roads upgrading and sealing, and rural electrification program.",""],[1,"14","12","Introduction of Level 4 District Hospitals","with strategic investments in the secondary health services and improved health systems in the Districts through the introduction of Level 4 District Hospitals in every Districts of the country.",""],[1,"14","13","Upgrade Port Moresby and Angau Hospitals to Level 7 Super Specialist Hospitals","To invest in upgrading the Port Moresby and Angau Hospitals to Level 7 Super Specialist Hospitals so they are equipped to provide diagnostic services for early detection and treatment of cancers, heart and other diseases to prevent many unnecessary losses of lives.",""],[1,"14","13","New Provincial Hospital Construction and Hospital Upgrading Programme","We are also building the new Enga and Central Provincial Hospitals and upgrading others around the country;",""],[1,"53","13","Special Medical Services and Hospital Upgrading Programme","The Government will provide better health services which are closer to people through establishment of Special Medical Services, new Boram and Enga Hospitals, upgrading of District Hospitals to Level 4 in all Districts and improvement of higher level of medical services at Provincial Hospitals with training of more health personnel.",""],[1,"54","12","Health Service Access and Efficiency Improvement","the Government's plan is to make \"quality health services accessible and efficient\" over the next five years.",""],[1,"59","10","Health Facility Upgrading Programme","Upgrade district health center to district hospitals (Level 4) provincial hospitals to Level 5, 4 regional hospitals to Level 6, and referral hospital (Angau and POMGH) to Level 7 status.",""],[1,"59","12","Rollout of Provincial Health Authorities","Roll out of Provincial Health Authorities (PHA) and strengthen Community Health Posts (CHP) throughout the country.",""],[1,"59","12","Strengthening of Community Health Posts","Roll out of Provincial Health Authorities (PHA) and strengthen Community Health Posts (CHP) throughout the country.",""],[1,"60","16","Town Districts Health Centre Upgrading Programme","All 89 Town Districts Health Centres are upgraded to District Hospitals by 2022",""],[1,"77","5","Social Sector Funding Allocation","In total, health, education, community and culture will be allocated K5.1 billion to build district hospitals, health centres, sports facilities and fund other social programmes.",""]],"37":[[2,"100","1","HIV Treatment Service Expansion","There have been improvements in the roll out of treatment services",""],[2,"100","1","Prevention of Mother-to-Child HIV Transmission","and programs such as HIV prevention to reduce HIV transmission from parent to child;",""],[2,"100","1","HIV Counselling and Testing Site Expansion","increased number of counselling and testing sites;",""],[2,"100","1","HIV Awareness and Workplace Policy Initiative","awareness and work place policy on HIV/AIDS.",""],[2,"100","2","HIV Prevention, Testing, Treatment, Care and Support Programme","The overall strategy for this sector over the next five (5) years will focus on prevention programs, counselling, testing, treatment, care and support services.",""],[2,"100","2","HIV and Sexual Health Strategy 2018-2020","Efforts to tackle the HIV/AIDS epidemic will be guided by the new HIV and Sexual Health Strategy 2018-2020 which envisages for considerable focus to assist people with HIV to know their HIV status and access clinical monitoring, treatment care and support.",""],[2,"101","18","Epidemic Surveillance and Awareness Strengthening","Strengthen surveillance system and awareness to better understand the characteristics and levels of the epidemic among the population.",""],[2,"101","20","National Care and Treatment Services Scale-Up","Scale up care and treatment services throughout the country.",""],[2,"101","22","HIV/AIDS Awareness and Prevention Mainstreaming","HIV/AIDS awareness and prevention to be mainstreamed in schools, workplaces and communities.",""],[2,"101","23","Prevention of Mother-to-Child Transmission (PMTCT) and Referral Support","Eliminate missed opportunities to provide pregnant women with ART and referrals of infants to paediatric treatment sites.",""],[2,"101","25","National Response to Reduce Gender Inequalities and HIV Vulnerability","Institutionalise national response to reduce gender inequalities that contribute to PNG's high level vulnerability to the HIV/AIDS epidemic.",""],[2,"101","27","Education and Awareness Programs for High Schools","Implement education and awareness programs (Coverage of high schools)",""],[2,"101","28","HIV/AIDS Awareness Activities at Public Events","Implement awareness of HIV/AIDS activities during national and local social, cultural, sporting, and professional events (Coverage in local and national events)",""],[2,"101","29","Expansion of Registered Voluntary Counselling and Testing Sites","Extend coverage of registered Voluntary Counselling Testing sites",""],[2,"101","30","PMTCT Integration into ART Guidelines","Incorporate PMTCT into new ART guidelines.",""],[2,"101","31","HIV/AIDS Workplace Policy Development","5. Develop HIV/AIDS workplace policy (Coverage of workplace policies in the public sector)",""]],"39":[[1,"15","4","Air Capability Enhancement for Disaster Response and EEZ Patrol","To improve the air capabilities of the Defence Force to respond quickly and more effectively to natural disasters and patrol our vast Exclusive Economic Zone (EEZ);",""],[1,"61","5","National Security Enhancement and Defence Force Capability Strengthening","Enhance national security and strengthen PNG Defence Force air, land and naval capabilities.",""],[1,"61","8","Strengthening National Security Organisations","In the medium term, the Government plans to strengthen the existing national security organisations that are responsive to security threats, natural disasters and providing emergency relief services, infrastructure development, border patrols and maritime surveillance.",""],[1,"61","8","Modernisation of Defence Air, Land and Naval Forces","The PNG Defence air, land and naval forces need to be modernised to handle complex security challenges at national, regional and international levels.",""],[1,"61","8","National Security Personnel Training and Skills Development","The national security personnel need to be skilled and trained to handle threats posed by high-powered weapons used in crimes and ethnic and electoral violence, as well as technologically-operated systems.",""],[1,"62","1","National Security Capability Enhancement","The Government plans to enhance PNG's National Security capabilities in line with the National Security Policy and Action Plan 2014-2020.",""],[1,"62","1","National Security Policy and Action Plan Implementation Framework","The Policy provides the strategic framework for security oversight, coordination, alignment and guidance for the security agencies to effectively carry out their functions.",""],[1,"62","20","National Security Agency Capacity Strengthening","Improve capacity of national security agencies to fully implement national security policy agenda.",""],[1,"62","21","Border Security Infrastructure Development","Establish appropriate border security infrastructure on land, air and sea to provide national security.",""],[1,"62","22","National Security Agency Operational Capacity Improvement","Improve operational capacity of national security agencies to ensure effective border surveillance and security management",""],[1,"63","4","Wutung Border Post Operationalization","Operationalize Wutung Border Post - Improve Defence Air Capabilities",""],[1,"63","4","Defence Air Capability Improvement","Operationalize Wutung Border Post - Improve Defence Air Capabilities",""],[2,"80","1","National Security Policy and Defence White Paper","The government has taken a step further to produce the country's first National Security Policy (NSP) together with the first home-grown Defence White Paper since 1999.",""],[2,"80","1","National Security Coordination and Early Warning Strengthening","They are intended to improve national security coordination and enhance early warning and response systems.",""],[2,"80","2","Modern Defence Force Development Programme","the Government has prioritized to develop a modern Defence Force, which includes development of infrastructure, new capabilities for Air, Navy, and Land forces and provide appropriate training that is compatible and resilient to meet its contemporary challenges and to fulfil its core functions mandated by the Constitution.",""],[2,"81","1","Defence Force Development and Emergency Relief Support","To develop a vibrant Defence Force that is responsive to national defence and security needs; and attend to national call for urgent infrastructure development, natural disaster and emergency relief services for the country.",""],[2,"81","11","Defence Force Recruitment, Training and Development","Continue to recruit, train and develop the Defence force.",""],[2,"81","13","Border Security Infrastructure and Capability Development","Develop and build the land, air and sea capabilities and appropriate border security infrastructure",""],[2,"81","14","Strengthen Bilateral and Border Security Arrangements","Strengthen existing bilateral and security arrangements that aims to promote PNG sovereignty and strengthen its borders",""],[2,"81","15","Military Support for Nation-Building and Emergency Response","Effectively utilize the military in nation building tasks, civil emergency and international obligations",""],[2,"81","16","Border Security Regulatory Agency Cooperation Mechanism","Strengthen the cooperation and partnership between regulatory agencies associated with border security.",""],[2,"81","17","National Security Policy and Legislation Reform","Improve policy and legislation covering all aspects of national security.",""],[2,"81","18","National Security Administration Training Programme","Scale up training programs associated with the administration of national security.",""],[2,"81","19","Military Aircraft and Helicopter Procurement","Purchase of 4 PAC 750 Military Aircrafts/Helicopters",""]],"40":[[2,"89","1","Border Management System Rollout","Since 2010, Immigration and Citizen Authority (ICA) continued its successful rollout of the Border Management System (BMS) to all PNG diplomatic Missions and Posts abroad.","Immigration and Citizen Authority (ICA)"],[2,"89","1","Provincial and Border Office Establishment","ICA established new provincial and border offices at strategic locations throughout the country.","Immigration and Citizen Authority (ICA)"],[2,"89","1","National Refugee Policy Implementation","The authority has also reached a significant milestone in 2015 with the implementation of PNG National Refugee Policy.","Immigration and Citizen Authority (ICA)"],[2,"90","11","Unified Visa and Work Permit Service","Consolidate and streamline visa and work permit into a single product and only one agency, ICA to make it easier for skilled workers, business people, tourists and former citizens to come in.",""],[2,"90","13","Visa Reform to Ease Employment and Business Entry and Exit Barriers","Ease entry/exit barriers for employment and business.",""],[2,"90","15","Establishment of Regional Immigration Offices","Establish 4 regional immigration offices to bring services closer to the people and reduce congested timeframe for processing visas.",""],[2,"90","17","Integrated Border Management System Procurement and IT Infrastructure Upgrade","Improve IT systems and infrastructure in all ICA offices with procurement of integrated border management system",""],[2,"90","19","Annual Immigration Enforcement Review and Removal Exercise","Quarterly review and removal exercise conducted annually by Immigration Task Force to remove overstayed persons, persons breaching visa conditions, violate PNG constitution and exploit natural resources.",""],[2,"90","21","National Refugee Policy Implementation","Full implementation of National Refugee Policy to take the proactive role in managing refugee issues",""],[2,"90","24","BMS System Installation for Overseas Missions and Provincial Offices","Install BMS system to all overseas missions and provincial offices,",""]],"41":[[1,"17","2","Revenue Base Expansion and Revenue Collection Improvement","Under the MTDP III, the Government will focus on: (1) Increasing the revenue base and improving revenue collection,",""],[1,"20","4","Domestic Revenue Mobilization","Increase the internal revenue on a sustainable basis to secure sufficient resources from domestic tax collections, non-tax revenues and export earnings;",""],[1,"20","9","Provincial and District Internal Revenue Mobilization Support","Support provinces and districts to generate sustainable internal revenue;",""],[1,"42","1","Internal Revenue Mobilization Support for Provinces and Districts","Provinces and Districts will be encouraged and supported to increase their revenue to support their service delivery and development initiatives.",""],[1,"45","4","Tax Base Broadening and Compliance Improvement","The focus of the Government is to broaden the tax base through improved tax compliance and the capacity of revenue generating institutions and State Owned Enterprises (SOEs).",""],[1,"48","7","Revenue Collection Efficiency and Compliance Strengthening","Improve efficiency and strengthen compliance in revenue collection across all state agencies and levels of government, and the private sector.",""],[1,"76","3","Revenue-Raising Agency Funding Support","Furthermore, sufficient funding is envisaged for major revenue raising agencies, IRC and PNG Customs Service.",""]],"42":[[1,"67","12","Fiscal Planning and Expenditure Management Strengthening","Strengthen fiscal planning and expenditure management by adhering to principles laid out in the medium-term fiscal strategies.",""],[1,"76","2","Medium-Term Fiscal Strategy for MTDP III Implementation","The fiscal envelope for implementation of MTDP III is outlined in the Medium Term Fiscal Strategy 2018-2022 (MTFS), which contains Medium Term Revenue Strategy (MTRS) and Medium Term Debt Strategy (MTDS).",""],[1,"76","2","Stringent Fiscal Management Framework","The framework calls for stringent fiscal management, while the amended 2006 Public Finance Management Act 2017 sets legal requirements for maintaining sustainable debt level at maximum level of 35% of GDP and reducing it to 30% of GDP by 2022.",""],[1,"76","3","Public Investment for Revenue-Generating Capacity","Public investment will be focused on building revenue generating capacities.",""],[1,"79","11","Public Finance Management Act Review","The Government is reviewing the Public Finance Management Act (PFMA) to accommodate the relevant changes in public finance management.",""],[1,"79","13","Public Expenditure and Financial Accountability Assessment","The Government through the Department of Finance is also undertaking Public Expenditure and Financial Accountability (PEFA) Assessment.","Department of Finance"]],"43":[[2,"83","1","Unified Budget and Medium-Term Fiscal Planning","The government has strengthened its fiscal planning and expenditure management by adhering to principles laid out in the medium-term fiscal strategies with the integration of recurrent and development budgets into a unified budget since 2015.",""],[2,"83","1","Multiyear Budgeting Implementation","Efforts towards the implementation of the multiyear budgeting is expected to further improve medium term expenditure planning and prioritization.",""],[2,"83","2","Public Service Performance Enhancement Measures","Robust measures will be undertaken in the medium term to combat these issues crippling the public services.",""],[2,"83","2","Transparent and Accountable Public Service Reform","These measures will be undertaken with a view to ensure that the Government develops an effective and efficient public service that is transparent and accountable at all levels.",""]],"44":[[1,"97","1","DSIP and PSIP Expenditure Monitoring and Evaluation","Significant development expenditure of K1, 335m is budgeted annually through the DSIP and PSIP which must be strictly monitored and evaluated periodically for value of money and its impacts to service delivery.","DNPM | Department of Implementation and Rural Development (DIRD)"],[1,"97","1","SIP Funding Tracking and Optimization Mechanism","DNPM in collaboration with the Department of Implementation and Rural Development (DIRD) and other central agencies should work together to ensure that SIP funding is tracked regularly, optimized and producing tangible benefits to the people and to the country as a whole.","DNPM | Department of Implementation and Rural Development (DIRD) | other central agencies"],[1,"100","1","Expenditure Control and Reconciliation Strengthening","Strengthening reconciliation between human resources, physical progress of projects and financial systems is necessary for successful execution of the capital budget in the medium and long term.",""],[1,"100","2","Contingency Buffer Funding for Public Investment Projects","Hence, PIP projects need to have buffer funding appropriated in the budget solely for such unforeseen circumstances.",""]],"45":[[1,"68","8","Procurement System Reform","Implement effective Procurement system",""],[1,"78","6","Prudent Project Planning and Monitoring","The Government will undertake prudent planning approach and thorough monitoring of the projects implementation to optimise the expenditure and maximise the outcome of the investments.",""],[1,"79","12","Procurement Policy and Procurement Law","The Government is also working on Procurement Policy and Procurement Law.",""],[1,"80","1","Integrated Financial Management System Rollout","The Government is also rolling out the Integrated Financial Management System (IFMS).",""]],"46":[[2,"85","1","National Statistical System Transformation Strategy","The government has undertaken the first step to transform National Statistical System (NSS) in the country through the formulation of the Papua New Guinea Strategy for the Development of Statistics (PNGSDS) 2017-2026 to increase the availability of high quality, timely and reliable data.",""],[2,"85","3","National Statistical System Coordination and Capacity Strengthening","The focus for NSS in the medium term is to strengthen the coordination of the NSS, develop human resource capacity of the NSS, strengthen the quality of the NSS products, promote dissemination, accessibility, and utilize of statistical information.",""],[2,"86","13","National Statistical System Coordination Strengthening","Strengthening the coordination of the National Statistical System (NSS)",""],[2,"86","17","Implementation and Funding for the Papua New Guinea Strategy for the Development of Statistics","Advocate implementation and funding for the Strategy for the development of Statistics (PNGSDS)",""],[2,"86","18","NSS Coordination Structure","1. Establish NSS Coordination structure",""],[2,"86","21","Improved Statistical Collection Methodologies","Use proper statistical collection methodologies for statistical activities",""],[2,"86","27","National Statistical System Establishment and NSO Reform","NSO Reform (Establish NSS, review legislations, capacity, statistical methodologies developed)",""]],"47":[[2,"85","1","National Identification Project","The Government has also initiated the NID project that captures all information of all its citizens including development, population data and accessing other vital services for development and sustainable growth.",""]],"48":[[2,"84","4","Public Institution Monitoring and Evaluation Mechanisms","Develop monitoring and evaluation mechanisms to ensure public institutions become accountable.",""],[2,"110","19","Public Institution Monitoring and Evaluation Mechanisms","Develop monitoring and evaluation mechanisms to ensure public institutions become accountable.",""],[2,"113","13","MTDP III Monitoring and Evaluation Readiness Assessment","Assess readiness and capacity of key sectors, departments, agencies, provinces, districts and other partners to implement the MTDP III M&E process",""],[2,"113","14","Sector and Agency M&E Framework Development","Develop & enhance the Sector/Agency M&E framework/plan and/or performance assessment frameworks",""],[2,"113","19","Provincial and District M&E Framework Development and Enhancement","3.2 Develop & enhance the Provincial & District M&E framework/plan or performance assessment frameworks",""],[2,"113","22","M&E Toolkit Pilot","Piloting of M&E toolkit with selected provinces and districts",""],[2,"113","26","Sector M&E Working Groups and Agency M&E Units Strengthening","3.4 Establishment and/or strengthening of Sector M&E Working Groups and Agency M&E units",""],[2,"114","3","MTDP III M&E Guidelines and Toolkit Development","Development of MTDP III M&E guidelines and toolkit",""],[2,"114","14","Routine Monitoring","Undertake routine monitoring",""],[2,"114","37","Advocacy, Communication, and M&E Culture Institutionalization","Institutionalizing advocacy, communication and promoting M&E culture within DNPM and external audience",""],[2,"114","40","National Data Collection Centre Establishment","Setting up of the National Data Collection Centre",""]],"49":[[1,"91","15","Establishment and Strengthening of M&E Steering and Coordination Committees","Establishing and strengthening the M&E Steering Committees (SCs), Sector Coordination Committees (SCCs) or Coalition of Partners (COPs) and other sector management or technical teams as the networks of planning, review, reporting, coordination, and communication between DNPM technical secretariat and the sector agencies and provinces (Coordination);",""],[1,"94","1","Multi-Stakeholder M&E Coordination and Communication Mechanism","The M&E Plan relies on coordination among government agencies at all levels, private sector, civil society organisations, and other development partners.",""],[1,"94","2","MTDP III Coordination and Performance Reporting Mechanism","The DNPM technical secretariat will work closely with the Sector Committees (SCs), Sector Working Groups (SWGs), and Coalition of Partners (COPs) which will be organised and/or strengthened, to share sector data, monitor performance and report on MTDP III implementation.",""],[1,"94","2","MTDP III Evaluation and Annual Performance Reporting","These groups will provide technical support to the DNPM technical secretariat during annual, mid-term, final evaluation of the MTDP III implementation.",""],[1,"94","2","Inclusive Coordination Group Membership for Development Partners and Stakeholders","Development Partners (private sector, multilateral and bilateral partners, CKRAs, etc.) and other stakeholders will be invited to become members of the coordination groups.",""],[1,"99","1","Stakeholder-Inclusive MTDP III Planning and Coordination","To ensure stakeholder ownership and accountability, all relevant sectors, departments, agencies and committees will be involved in the planning, implementation, coordination, management, monitoring, evaluation and reporting of the MTDP III.",""],[1,"99","1","Periodic Review and Collaborative M&E Leadership","DNPM will provide leadership in periodic reviews and other M&E collaborative activities to build effective and harmonious relationships among stakeholders at all levels, and further promote economic and social development.","DNPM"],[1,"99","3","Prioritized and Sequenced Funding for Strategies, Programmes and Projects","DNPM will work closely with key executing agencies to prioritise and sequence funding to deliver strategies, programmes and projects.",""]],"51":[[2,"58","1","KITE Program Investment Expansion","Under MTDP III, and in implementing the Science Technology and Innovation (STI) Plan, the Government will increase its investment in this sector through the annual budget support for the KITE Program.",""],[2,"59","27","National Innovation System Establishment","Establish Papua New Guinea's National Innovation System and Strengthened partnerships",""],[2,"59","29","Research and Development Investment Mobilization","Mobilize and increase Research and Development Investments",""]],"52":[[1,"37","1","Protected Areas Investment Programme","The focus in the medium term is to invest in protected areas, support waste management activities, and maintain PNG's biodiversity.",""],[1,"37","1","Waste Management Support Activities","The focus in the medium term is to invest in protected areas, support waste management activities, and maintain PNG's biodiversity.",""],[1,"71","9","Biodiversity Conservation for Tourism and Species Protection","Improve biodiversity conservation for tourism purposes and protection of PNG's diverse flora and fauna.",""],[1,"71","10","StaRS Principle 1 Environmental Cost Internalization Enforcement","Enforce the implementation of the StaRS principle 1 associated with protecting the environment by shifting responsibility to polluters to internalise environmental cost through setting standards for penalties and fees.",""],[1,"71","11","Waste Management Regulation Compliance Improvement","Improve compliance of industry and municipals/urban centres for waste management regulation.",""],[1,"71","12","Environmental Monitoring and Reporting Improvement","Improve monitoring and reporting of environmental issues and behavioural trends.",""],[1,"71","13","Sustainable Use of Non-Renewable Natural Assets","5. Promote sustainable uses of non-renewable natural assets in forestry, marine, minerals and bio-diversity.",""],[1,"71","14","University Human Capital and Environmental Awareness Programmes","Support human capital development educational, research and other environmental awareness programmes in universities aimed at developing capacities to transition to sustainable development modes of growth.",""],[2,"104","2","Protected Areas Investment","Hence, the focus for the medium term is to invest in protected areas and support waste management initiatives to ensure that PNG maintains its biodiversity.",""],[2,"104","2","Waste Management Support Initiative","Hence, the focus for the medium term is to invest in protected areas and support waste management initiatives to ensure that PNG maintains its biodiversity.",""],[2,"105","12","Biodiversity Conservation for Tourism and Species Protection","Improve biodiversity conservation for the purposes of tourism and also for protecting and maintaining PNG's diverse flora and fauna.",""],[2,"105","14","StaRS Environmental Compliance Enforcement","Enforce the Implementation of principles prescribed by StaRS to protect the environment by shifting responsibility to polluters to internalise environmental cost through setting standards for penalties and fees.",""],[2,"105","16","Waste Management Compliance Improvement","Improve compliance of industry and municipals for waste management regulations.",""],[2,"105","18","Environmental Monitoring and Reporting Improvement","Improve monitoring and reporting of environmental issues and trends.",""],[2,"105","23","Polluter Pays Legislation Standards and Regulations","Develop standards and regulations for a polluter pay legislation to be enacted and enforced",""],[2,"105","26","Plastic Bag Ban Compliance Monitoring","Monitor and ensure compliance of ban on plastic bags",""]],"53":[[1,"69","5","Disaster Reduction Planning and Early Warning System","Effective disaster reduction planning, early warning system and emergency response strategy are needed.",""],[1,"69","5","Stakeholder Agency Capacity Building for Disaster Response","Building capacity in the various stakeholder agencies should be the priority of Government as we move into the future so that we are able to adequately respond to these challenges.",""],[1,"69","5","Disaster Coordination Mechanism Among Support Agencies","By 2022, the Government anticipates to have strong coordination amongst stakeholder support agencies to deal with disaster related matters.",""],[1,"72","4","Disaster Surveillance System","Establish disaster surveillance system in disaster prone locations.",""],[1,"72","5","Monitoring and Evaluation Capacity Strengthening for Early Warning","Improve the capacity of monitoring and evaluation mechanisms to predict geophysical threats in order to raise the scope for early warning.",""],[1,"72","6","Disaster Planning and Response Capacity Building","Build capacity to effectively plan and deal with natural disasters.",""],[1,"72","21","Disaster Mitigation Program","Implement the Disaster Mitigation Program",""],[1,"72","24","Fire Station Construction, Rehabilitation and Upgrading","7. Construction, Rehabilitation & Upgrading of 14 Fire Stations",""],[2,"108","1","Disaster Risk Management and Mitigation Support Programme","Hence, disaster risk management and mitigation programs will be supported over the medium term.",""],[2,"109","4","Building Standards Enforcement and Disaster Surveillance System","Implement and enforce building standards for the construction of infrastructure as well as establish disaster surveillance system in disaster prone areas.",""],[2,"109","6","Disaster Response Capacity Building","Build capacity to effectively deal with natural disasters.",""],[2,"109","8","International and Regional Cooperation and Local Partnership Support for Disaster Risk Management","Enhance International and Regional Cooperation and strengthen local partnerships for adequate and sustainable technical, capacity and funding support to compliment national NDRR/NDRM actions",""],[2,"109","10","Monitoring and Evaluation Capacity Strengthening for Early Warning","Improve the capacity of monitoring and evaluation mechanisms to predict geophysical threats in order to raise the scope of early warning.",""],[2,"109","15","Fire Station Establishment and Rehabilitation with Computer-Aided Dispatch System","Establish and rehabilitate fire stations with computer aided dispatch system installed at key locations",""],[2,"109","16","Internally Displaced Resettlement Policy","Develop Internally Displaced Resettlement Policy to assist communities displaced by natural-caused disasters",""],[2,"109","18","Integrated Disaster Loss Database Expansion","Establishment of Integrated Disaster Loss Database Profile for PNG expanded to all provinces.",""]],"54":[[2,"96","2","Youth Development Programs","The focus for youth in the medium term is to support youth development programs and create an enabling environment for youth to be engaged in economic activities that will sustain their lives.",""],[2,"97","13","Youth Engagement Policy and Administrative Reform","Improve policies, legislations and administration to enhance support for youth engagement in economic growth and social development.",""],[2,"97","15","Education and Skills Training for Employment and Self-Employment","Improve and increase education and skills training and personal development programs that meets job market needs and for self-employment.",""],[2,"97","17","Employment Opportunity Expansion","Improve and increase employment opportunities in the public and private sectors.",""],[2,"97","19","Youth Civic Engagement and Democratic Participation Support","Support youth in civic engagements and democratic participation processes in schools, communities, institutions and society.",""],[2,"97","21","Youth Policy Development and Implementation","Develop and implement the Youth Policy",""],[2,"97","22","Youth Council Network Strengthening","Establish and strengthen youth council networks",""],[2,"97","23","Establish Provincial Youth Friendly Centres","3. Establish Provincial Youth Friendly Centres",""],[2,"97","24","National Youth Database Establishment","4. Establish national youth database",""]],"55":[[1,"33","7","Whole-of-Government Development Coordination Approach","A whole of government approach with development partners and key stakeholders such as churches, is required to streamline all development activities to achieve the economies of scale needed.",""],[1,"65","1","Private Sector and Community Stakeholder Partnership Strengthening","Strengthen partnerships with the private sector and community- based stakeholders to address service delivery and development.",""],[1,"81","5","Strategic Partnerships and Development Cooperation Coordination Policy","Fostering partnerships and development cooperation: Build strategic alliances, economic cooperation and establish partnership between all stakeholders.",""],[1,"82","2","Development Cooperation Policy 2018-2022","The new PNG Development Cooperation Policy 2018-2022 focuses on strengthening development cooperation effectiveness and it is about ensuring that optimal results are achieved through effective coordination between the Government and our Development Partners into the medium term.",""],[1,"82","2","Government Control of Development Cooperation Resources","This Government's approach is to take greater control of the management of development cooperation resources, mobilise and strengthen partnerships, apply effective delivery modalities and explore innovative partnership approaches.",""],[1,"82","4","Programme-Based Development Cooperation Approach","PNG is keen to apply this approach.",""],[1,"83","2","Private Sector Partnership Recognition and PPP Promotion Measures","The Government plans to take appropriate measures to formally recognise these contributions in its planning, coordination, programming and evaluation processes.",""],[1,"83","2","Public-Private Partnership Advancement","The Government is keen to progress PPPs due to the emergence of and impact of companies, such as Mainland Holdings, in poultry and dairy sub-sectors; PNG Biomass in the energy sector working together with relevant institutions of Government, and looking into and accelerating state equity into potential private sector investments that are supporting MTDP III priorities.",""],[1,"83","4","South-South Collaboration for Trade, Investment, and Knowledge Exchange","PNG is ready to form specific collaborations in these areas to boost PNG's economic growth and service delivery priorities.",""],[1,"83","5","Trilateral Cooperation Promotion","Government is looking to promote new and innovative solutions for PNG's development priorities, embrace international best practices and experiences from other countries with similar goals and ambitions.",""],[1,"84","1","Multi-stakeholder Sectoral Dialogue and Review Mechanism","Multi-stakeholder sectoral dialogues and reviews will be promoted widely for all MTDP III priority sectors",""],[2,"91","2","Aid Coordination and Integration into Government Planning and Budgeting System","Thus, it had become necessary for the Government of Papua New Guinea to effectively coordinate and integrate assistance from various development partners into the Government Planning and Budgeting System and consistent with its rolling Medium Term Development Plan (MTDP).",""],[2,"91","3","Development Cooperation Policy Framework","the Government introduced its inaugural \"2015 PNG Development Cooperation Policy (DCP)\" which is a framework that provides a clear direction and defines the protocols of engagement with development partners in mobilizing, coordinating, managing and delivering development assistance in PNG.",""],[2,"91","4","Development Partnerships and Strategic Collaboration Framework","This new poIicy will build on the current traditional Development Partnerships, establish new bilateral and multilateral partnerships, critical and strategic collaborations with the Private Sector, Philanthropic Agencies and Civil Society to enable a bigger force of energy for development.",""],[2,"92","14","Foreign Aid Management Strengthening","Elevate/Strengthen the status of Foreign Aid management to effectively manage all matters related to foreign aid extended by development partners as well as to deliver development assistance to PICS strategically to realize goals set under \"PNG Development Cooperation Policy\" and \"PNG Pacific Cooperation Strategy\".",""],[2,"92","16","Development Cooperation Policy Procedures Manual","Develop comprehensive procedures manual to fully operationalize the PNG Development Cooperation Policy.",""],[2,"92","18","Development Assistance Information System","Develop comprehensive development assistance information system to measure achievement of policy objectives set under PNG Development Cooperation Policy",""],[2,"92","20","Trade in Aid Mainstreaming Strategy","Mainstream Trade into Aid as a key strategy to maximize impact of assistance for economic benefit.",""],[2,"92","22","Implementation of Reviewed DCP","Implementation of reviewed DCP",""],[2,"92","24","Country Partnership Strategies for Development Partnerships","Country Partnership Strategies established for all Development Partnerships with PNG",""],[2,"92","26","PNG Pacific Cooperation Strategy Implementation","PNG Pacific Cooperation Strategy is endorsed and implemented",""],[2,"92","27","Development Assistance Information System Utilization","Development Assistance Information System (DAISy) is effectively utilized",""],[2,"92","28","Establishment of Development Corporation Office in New York and Canberra Aid Office","Establishment of Development Corporation Office in New York and Canberra Aid Office",""],[2,"123","2","Development Partner Dialogue and Consultation Mechanism","Constant dialogue and consultation with development partners help resolve sector issues and assist sector during mobilisation.",""]],"56":[[1,"10","5","Private Sector Partnership for Critical Investment Mobilization","we will continue our efforts to partner the private sector to secure critical investments that will create more jobs for our citizens, increase our exports and replace imports resulting in significant increase in our internal revenues.",""],[1,"40","1","Public-Private Partnership Strengthening for SOE Performance","Over the next five years (2018-2022), the target will be to reinforce the public-private partnerships (PPP) to improve efficiency and overall performance of the SOEs, with the overarching objective of delivering goods and services to improve livelihoods across the country at high quality and affordable prices.",""],[1,"81","3","Public-Private Partnership Initiatives for High-Impact Projects","Pursue and utilise public private partnership initiatives to support the economic growth strategies and delivery of high impact projects need to be harnessed.",""],[1,"81","7","Joint Government and Private Sector Investment Monitoring","These investments will be subjected to stringent management and close monitoring by the government and the private sector.",""]],"57":[[1,"39","6","State-Owned Enterprise Reform and Support Programme","The Government intends to continue investment in equity and support the SOEs with necessary reforms to be commercially viable.",""],[1,"40","10","State-Owned Enterprise Repositioning and Restructuring Programme","Over the medium term, the Government aims to reposition and restructure the SOEs to become very competitive in the market and achieving high level of efficiency and profitability.",""],[1,"48","8","State Equity Expansion Through SOEs in Strategic Investment Areas","Increase uptake of state-equity through SOEs in strategic investment areas in both renewable and non-renewable sectors of the economy.",""],[1,"48","9","Provincial Business Arms Restructuring Programme","Reposition and restructure provincial business arms to become competitive, efficient and profitable whilst supporting government efforts in service delivery",""]],"58":[[2,"15","2","Coffee Quality Improvement and Plantation Rehabilitation Programme","Therefore, the industry will focus on improving the quality of coffee, rehabilitating the plantations and containing the CBB.",""],[2,"15","11","Coffee Block and Plantation Revitalization","Revive large coffee blocks and plantations",""],[2,"15","13","Extension, Training, and Business Support Services for Cooperatives and Smallholder Farmers","Provide extension/training/Business support services to cooperatives and smallholder farmers (SMEs, Youth and Women)",""],[2,"15","15","Internationally Certified Coffee Mills for Cooperatives","Establish internationally certified coffee mills for cooperatives to attract premium prices and ensure quality",""],[2,"15","19","Coffee Value Addition and Domestic Consumption Promotion","Promote value adding products and domestic consumption of coffee",""],[2,"15","27","Green Energy, Digital Agriculture, and E-Marketing Support for Coffee Industry","Promote green energy, digital agriculture and e-marketing in coffee industry",""],[2,"16","3","Coffee Industry Infrastructure Development Program","Coffee Industry Infrastructure Development Program",""]],"59":[[2,"17","2","Cocoa Tree Planting and Export Yield Expansion Plan","The Government, under this plan, aims to plant 13 million new cocoa trees and increase PNG's current export yield of 40,000 metric tonnes to 160,000 metric tonnes by 2022.",""],[2,"17","11","Regional Nurseries and Seed Gardens Development","Establish & Improve Regional nurseries and seed gardens i.e. Momase, Southern and NGI",""],[2,"17","13","Cocoa Plantation Rehabilitation Programme","Facilitate the rehabilitation of cocoa plantations and senile cocoa farms",""],[2,"17","17","Priority Road and Jetty Infrastructure Identification and Advisory Support","Facilitate, Identify and Advise on priority areas for road & jetty infrastructure",""],[2,"18","1","Establishment of Regional Nurseries","1. Establishment of regional nurseries",""],[2,"18","8","Cocoa Industry Capacity Improvement","8. Improve the capacity of the cocoa industry",""]],"60":[[2,"19","1","Bogia Coconut Syndrome Control and Coconut Sector Diversification","With these challenges, the Government aims to address the BCS disease through the relocation of the gene bank from Madang to Milne Bay Province and to improve the productivity and diversification of the coconut products.",""],[2,"19","14","Coconut Industry Capacity Strengthening","Build and strengthen the coconut industry's capacity",""],[2,"19","22","Coconut Plantation Rehabilitation Programme","Rehabilitate coconut plantations",""],[2,"20","1","High-Value Coconut Product MSME Development and Marketing","Establish new MSMEs on processing of High Value Coconut Products and Marketing",""],[2,"20","2","Central Coconut Nursery Establishment and Maintenance","Establish and maintain central coconut nurseries for 14 provinces",""],[2,"20","3","Regional Resource Centre Establishment","3. Establish 3 resource centres per region",""],[2,"20","4","Plantation Rehabilitation Programme","Rehabilitate 2 abandoned plantations per region",""],[2,"20","5","Relocation of the International Gene Bank for the South Pacific","Relocate the International Gene bank for the South Pacific based in Madang to Milne Bay Province",""],[2,"20","6","Pest Containment Protocols for BCS and Coconut Rhinoceros Beetle","Develop and implement protocols for containment of BCS and coconut rhinoceros beetle in 14 provinces.",""]],"61":[[2,"21","1","Rubber Production Expansion and Downstream Processing Promotion","Rubber industry aims to increase rubber production by promoting downstream processing and encouraging more farmers to venture into the industry.",""],[2,"21","12","PNG Rubber Industry Investment Expansion","Increase investments in the PNG rubber industry",""],[2,"21","14","SME Expansion in the PNG Rubber Industry","Increase number of SMEs in the PNG rubber industry",""],[2,"21","19","Rubber Block Rehabilitation","2. Rehabilitate Rubber blocks",""]],"62":[[2,"22","1","National Rice Policy 2015-2030","The PNG National Rice Policy 2015-2030 aims to change this situation and make PNG become a rice producer and exporter.",""],[2,"22","2","Domestic Commercial Rice Production Industry Development","Domestic commercial rice production industry is established in partnership with private sector and small scale farmers to reduce the volume of imported rice and meet growing",""],[2,"22","14","Private Sector Partnership for Production Cost Subsidies","Promote partnership with private sectors to subsidize costs in production",""],[2,"22","15","Large-Scale Rice Development Support Programme","Acquire land for large scale rice development, invest in appropriate and adequate research and development for quality improvement, and provide extension and training in rice development.",""],[2,"22","18","Economic Corridor Infrastructure and Utilities Development","Develop economic corridors through provision of infrastructure and utilities",""]],"63":[[2,"23","1","Cattle Breeding Investment Programme","Hence, the Government aims to invest significantly in the industry through cattle breeding programs.",""],[2,"23","11","Breeding and Distribution Centres Establishment","Establish breeding and distribution centres",""],[2,"23","15","Smallholder Commercial Pig and Poultry Production Support","Encourage Smallholder Commercial Pig and Poultry production",""],[2,"23","16","Cooperative Marketing under the Nucleus Estate Concept","Promote Cooperative Marketing under the Nucleus Estate Concept",""],[2,"24","11","National Food Security Council/Authority","Establish a National Food Security Council/Authority to guide, support and monitor implementation of PNG NFS 2016-2025",""],[2,"24","12","Hygiene, Nutrition and Dietary Education Programme","Support hygiene, nutrition and dietary education, programs and awareness among families, households and schools",""],[2,"24","13","Food Security Partnership Building","Establish partnerships among local, national and international stakeholders to food security and related concerns",""],[2,"24","14","Biosecurity Measures for Crop Protection","Put in place strong biosecurity measures to safeguard local food crops against pests and diseases",""],[2,"24","15","Agricultural Research and Development for Innovative Farming Methods","Support research and development for innovative farming methods against concerns like climate change",""],[2,"24","16","Baseline Establishment for Major Food and Livestock Crops and Products","Establishment of baseline of major food & livestock crop and products",""]],"64":[[2,"45","2","Mining Regulatory and Policy Framework","the Government will provide the regulatory and policy framework that is both simple but effective to keep industry compliance costs to a minimum to protect the environment and to ensure landowners and other stakeholders benefit.",""],[2,"45","2","Strengthening State Capacity for Mining Regulation Enforcement","This will be supported through strengthening the capacity of state institutions to administer and enforce mining regulations to ensure the Government's policy is implemented effectively;",""],[2,"45","2","Integrated Mine Development Approach","promote an integrated approach to mine development rather than an enclave approach;",""],[2,"45","2","Landowner Participation and Mining Stakeholder Mechanisms","develop and review appropriate mechanisms to address landowners' participation and industry issues;",""],[2,"45","2","Downstream Processing Promotion for Mining Value Addition","and pursue strategies under manufacturing and SME that encourage downstream processing to add value.",""],[2,"45","3","Support for Two New Mining Projects","The Government will support the development of two new mining projects in the medium term.",""],[2,"46","9","Enabling Environment for New Mining Projects","Provide the enabling environment for development of new mining projects",""],[2,"46","10","Simplified Regulatory and Policy Framework for Industry Compliance","Provide regulatory and policy framework that is both simple but effective to keep industry compliance costs to a minimum to 2 protect the environment and to ensure landowners and other stakeholders benefit",""],[2,"46","11","Regulatory Procedure Simplification for Exploration","Facilitate further exploration by simplifying and speeding up regulatory procedures",""],[2,"46","12","Mining Regulation Administration and Enforcement Capacity Strengthening","Strengthen the capacity of state institutions to administer and enforce mining regulations to ensure the Government's policy 4 is implemented effectively",""],[2,"46","13","Integrated Mine Development Approach","Promote an integrated approach to mine development rather than an enclave approach",""],[2,"46","14","Landowner Participation and Industry Issue Mechanisms","Develop and review appropriate mechanisms to address landowners' participation and industry issues",""],[2,"46","15","Downstream Processing Promotion for Manufacturing and SMEs","Pursue strategies under manufacturing and SME that encourage downstream processing to add value",""]],"65":[[2,"43","2","Strengthening State Institutions for Resource Governance","State institutions responsible for policy, administration, regulation, compliance and enforcement need to be strengthened.",""],[2,"43","2","Investment Framework Policy and Legislative Reform","The necessary policies and legislations that provide an investment framework for:",""],[2,"43","3","Third-Party Access for Strategic Gas Pipelines","Third party access for strategic gas pipelines and related infrastructure;",""],[2,"43","5","National Content Requirement for Oil and Gas Operations","Flexible and responsive national content requirement to ensure that oil and gas explorers and producers use a minimum amount of locally available and sourced labour and content in their operations in PNG need to be developed and implemented in the medium term.",""],[2,"43","6","Papua LNG Project Development","The Government will support the development of two new projects.",""],[2,"43","6","Pasca Gas Project Development","The Government will support the development of two new projects.",""],[2,"43","6","Gas Use for Electricity and Downstream Processing","It is also PNG's aim to use gas for electricity and for downstream processing in the future.",""],[2,"44","10","Enabling Environment for New Petroleum Projects","Provide the enabling environment for development of new petroleum projects",""],[2,"44","11","Continued Exploration Investment","Encourage continued investment in exploration",""],[2,"44","12","Strengthening of State Institutions for Policy and Regulatory Functions","Strengthen state institutions responsible for policy, administration, regulation, compliance and enforcement",""],[2,"44","14","Sovereign Wealth Fund Establishment","Establishment of SWF to provide equitable benefits for the current and future generations",""]],"66":[[1,"15","1","National Census Delivery","The focus is on delivering the 2020 National Census successfully, completing the NID Rollout by 2021 and implementing our National Strategy for Development of Statistics and Policy Monitoring and Evaluation Framework;",""],[1,"15","1","National ID Rollout Completion","The focus is on delivering the 2020 National Census successfully, completing the NID Rollout by 2021 and implementing our National Strategy for Development of Statistics and Policy Monitoring and Evaluation Framework;",""],[1,"15","1","National Statistics and Policy Monitoring Framework","The focus is on delivering the 2020 National Census successfully, completing the NID Rollout by 2021 and implementing our National Strategy for Development of Statistics and Policy Monitoring and Evaluation Framework;",""],[1,"66","4","National Identification System","The National Identification system will ease authentication difficulties faced today by identifying \"the person to be that person who claims to be\" through biometrics (finger prints, photo, and iris) captures.",""],[1,"66","6","Provincial Certificate and NID Card Registration and Printing","Undertaking registration and printing of certificates and NID cards at the provincial offices;",""],[1,"66","8","Civil Registration Legislation Reform","Working on the Civil Registration Legislation to give legal prominence to the PNG Civil & Identity System for identification and authentication of all users;",""],[1,"66","9","Integrated Government Information System Linkage and Complementation","Establishing links and complementation with the country's Integrated Government Information System (IGIS) that will store and transport all government information systems.",""],[1,"67","2","Centralised Civil and Identity Registry System","Develop a centralised civil and identity registry system",""],[1,"67","7","Provincial NID Office Establishment","6.9 Establish fully operational Provincial NID Offices.",""],[1,"67","8","District NID Office Operationalization","Establish fully operational District NID Offices.",""],[1,"67","16","Centralised Civil and Identity Registry System","Develop a centralised civil and identity registry system",""],[1,"67","17","Civil and Identity Registry Data Standardization","Customise all citizens/residents bio-data registration to be of the Civil & Identity Registry required data collection format.",""],[1,"67","18","Civil Registry Vital Events Registration","Register all Civil Registry Vital Events (births, adoption, marriages, divorces, migration and deaths) in the country.",""],[1,"67","19","Integration of Civil and Identity Registry with Government Services","Integrate PNG Civil & Identity Registry System to all other Government Services for authentication of Rollout out of Provincial and District NID registration Civil Registration Bill Passes by Parliament",""],[1,"67","21","Civil and Identity Registry Data Collection Standardization","Customise all citizens/residents bio-data registration to be of the Civil & Identity Registry required data collection format.",""],[1,"68","11","National Census Implementation","Implementation of the National Census in 2020 and Census Report by 2022.",""],[1,"74","18","National E-ID Card Program Implementation Intensification","Intensify the implementation of the National E-ID Card Program",""],[1,"74","20","2020 Population Census Support","Support the conduct of the 2020 Population Census",""]],"68":[[1,"10","3","Province and District Service Improvement Program","Province and District Service Improvement Program, Tuition Fee-Free education and Free Primary Health care program are currently addressing the development needs of our people.",""],[1,"11","5","District Offices Program","The MTDP III will focus on the following district programs: district hospitals, district offices, district town water supply systems, district town roads upgrading and sealing, and rural electrification program.",""],[1,"20","7","Rural Service Delivery Improvement","Improve quality of service delivery in rural districts across the country;",""],[1,"21","2","District Infrastructure and Economic Enablers Development","the MTDP III strives to bring development to district level, focusing on district infrastructure and district economic enablers - markets, roads and utilities, such as water, electricity, and telecommunication.",""],[1,"63","8","District Service Delivery Strengthening through District Development Authorities","the Government will focus on improving service delivery in the districts by optimising the use of the District Development Authorities as the frontline service delivery vehicle through strategic investments in district hospitals, court houses, police stations, markets, district communities and other social and economic facilities.",""],[1,"63","11","Sub-national Public Service Structure Development","The Government is determined to develop the structures at the sub-national levels to deliver public goods and services by providing funding support through the Service Improvement Programs (SIPs) whilst maintaining ongoing support to central and line agencies at the national level.",""],[1,"64","3","District Development Authority Capacity Building","The Government plans to support DDAs to be fully functional by 2022.",""],[1,"64","18","DDA Capacity Building for Service Delivery","5. Build capacity of DDAs for effective service delivery",""],[1,"65","9","District Development Authority Office Establishment","Establishment of District Development Authority Office",""],[1,"68","3","Rural Service Delivery and Local Governance Initiatives","Implement the Rural Service Delivery and Local Governance initiatives",""],[1,"77","4","District and Provincial Service Improvement Programs","Provinces remain the focus of the Government with continuous funding of Service Improvement Programs (DSIP and PSIP) and high impact provincial programs",""],[1,"77","4","Provincial Capital Investment Transfers","A total of K7.8 billion will be transferred to provinces over the medium term in form of capital investment",""],[1,"82","3","Sub-national Implementation of High-Impact Projects","Provinces and districts have a critical role to play in the implementation of high impact projects outlined in Part 2 of this plan.",""],[1,"82","3","Periodic Performance Reviews for Capital Investments","To improve the monitoring of capital investments, sub-national governments will institute periodic performance reviews at their level and report to the national government on their achievement of MTDP III priorities.",""]],"69":[[1,"10","3","Strategic Enabling Infrastructure Investment","Focus of our Plan is to grow the economy and to increase our internal revenue by 50%, building key strategic enabling infrastructure to unlock our economic potential, skill and create more jobs more business and wealth for our citizens.",""],[1,"10","5","Economic Sector Investment and Enabling Infrastructure Programme","In the MTDP III, we are focusing on increased investment in the economic sector to stimulate broad based economic growth.",""],[1,"11","3","Key Enabling Infrastructure Investment","To facilitate this economic sector stimulus, we are investing in key enabling infrastructures.",""],[1,"11","3","National Highway and Road Link Construction","We will construct five new national highways and missing road links to unlock the vast economic potential of our country.",""],[1,"15","6","Key Enabling Infrastructure Investment Programme","To invest in many key enabling infrastructures and reduce the cost of doing business.",""],[1,"49","28","Critical Transport Infrastructure Investment Programme","The Government will invest substantially in key and critical transport infrastructure to reduce cost of doing business and to expand and stimulate economic growth.",""],[1,"50","1","Transport and Port Infrastructure Development","Momase Highway, Central to Milne Bay Highway, Morobe to Gulf Highway, Baiyer to Madang Highway, new international wharves in Wewak, Kikori, Vanimo, Wewak and Manus, introduction of National Shipping Service, Nadzab Airport redevelopment, Madang, Wewak, Kavieng, Tari Airport redevelopment and new Kup Airport in Chimbu Province.",""],[1,"51","4","Rural Link Road and District Trunk Road Construction","Construct vital missing link roads and district trunk roads to strategic communities of economic potential for transportation of commodities like coffee, cocoa and tea to markets.",""],[1,"51","5","National Highway and Bridge Rehabilitation and Maintenance","Rehabilitate and maintain national highways including bridges which are identified that will contribute to economic growth.",""],[1,"51","6","Port and Wharf Rehabilitation and Upgrade Programme","Rehabilitate and upgrade major ports and strategic wharves and jetties along the coast and waterways",""],[1,"51","7","National Shipping Service with Government-Owned Fleets","Introduce National Shipping Service with Government-owned fleets.",""],[1,"51","14","Corridor Access and Connectivity Investments","These key investments will create access to improve flow of goods and services and movement of people to stimulate economic growth in each corridor.",""],[1,"51","16","Highlands Highway Rehabilitation","Rehabilitate the Highlands Highway to be in good and accessible condition, which is the lifeline for all economic activities in the Highland Region connecting major port in Lae and Madang.",""],[1,"51","18","Ports and Wharves Rehabilitation and Development","Key ports and wharves are rehabilitated and developed to open up access for goods and services.",""],[1,"51","20","Rural Airstrip Service Restoration and Improvement","To restore and improve services of rural airstrips",""],[1,"51","22","Major National Airport Upgrading Programme","To upgrade major national airports to improve and increase transportation of goods and services and movement of people.",""],[1,"51","24","Nadzab Airport Upgrade to Alternative International Airport","To upgrade the Nadzab (Lae) Airport to be an alternative international airport to Jackson's Airport (Port Moresby) by 2021.",""],[1,"53","1","New Kup Airport Construction","Construction of the new Kup Airport for the Chimbu Province to replace old Kundiawa Airport.",""],[1,"77","4","Transport Infrastructure Financing Program","Transport infrastructure is the key enabler for economic activities throughout the country and is projected for 19% of total financing (K5.1 billion)",""],[1,"77","4","Economic Corridor Roads and Missing Links Construction","MTDP III will fund new economic corridor roads and missing links, connecting coastal and inland provinces and drastically reducing logistical costs for business and public service delivery",""],[1,"79","9","Integrated Transport and Communication System Implementation","The proper implementation of ITCS will allow to deliver infrastructure development to rural areas, optimizing the cost and combining the efforts of the Government and private sector.",""],[1,"81","7","Transport Infrastructure Missing Links Development","Economic stimulus package and development of missing links in transport infrastructure will be vigorously pursued.",""],[1,"82","1","Inter-Provincial and Inter-District Corridor Development Projects","Viable inter-provincial corridor development (IPCD) or inter-district corridor development (IDCD) projects that serve as common socio-economic centres will be identified and developed for delivery of goods and services in provinces and districts.",""]],"70":[[1,"11","3","International Wharf Construction Programme","We will build four new international wharves to improve trade flows and provide markets for our produce.",""]],"71":[[1,"11","4","Regional Youth Business Incubation Centres","My Government will invest in new regional youth business incubation centres based on the highly successful Indian model.",""],[1,"11","4","Economic Stimulus Package for Job Creation","In addition, the economic stimulus package will provide the platform for more job opportunities for our people.",""],[1,"14","10","Regional Youth Business Incubation Centres","For the youths in particular, we will invest in regional youth business incubation centres to upskill and empower them to take up self-employment as an employment option;",""],[1,"20","5","Training, Capacity and Employment Opportunities for PNG Citizens","Increase training, capacity and employment opportunities for PNG citizens;",""],[1,"41","7","Citizen Training and Participation in Formal Business Sector","Citizen ownership and benefits in the formal business sector will be pursued with increase in training opportunities for citizens.",""],[1,"41","7","Youth Entrepreneurship and Productive Labour Force Development","Growth of population will be managed sustainably with youth to become active entrepreneurs and productive labour force.",""],[1,"48","17","TVET Training and Youth SME Promotion","Increase quality workforce through TVET training and encourage youth-based SMEs.",""],[1,"48","18","Youth Formal Employment Opportunities Expansion","11. Increase opportunities for youth engagement in formal employment.",""],[1,"53","15","Community Development Centres for Youth Skills and Employment","Youth skills trainings and access to employment will be facilitated through the establishment of Community Development Centres in every Districts.",""],[1,"55","1","Establishment of Provincial Youth Centres and District Community Development Centres","the Government plans to achieve its headline target of having a Skilled and Productive Youth by 2022 with establishment of Provincial Youth Centres and District Community Development Centres throughout the country",""],[1,"59","14","Education and Skills Training for Employment and Self-Employment","Improve and increase education and skills training and personal development programs that meet job market needs and for self- employment in SME type business ventures.",""]],"72":[[1,"11","1","Pacific Marine Industrial Zone Development","Pacific Marine Industrial Zone (PMIZ) in Madang will significantly increase the volume of processed marine products for domestic and export markets with creation of more employment opportunities.",""],[1,"11","1","Downstream Processing Expansion at Strategic Locations","The Government will expand and add value through downstream processing at strategic locations throughout the country.",""],[1,"42","1","Key Infrastructure Expansion and Land Development for Export Promotion","Key infrastructure will be expanded with development of more land with state equity to support export promotion and reduce imports and further efforts to improve law and order situation in the country.",""],[1,"48","15","Marine Industrial Zones Development","Develop Marine Industrial Zones (MIZs) to undertake offloading and onshore processing of PNG tuna.",""],[1,"48","21","Economic Corridors and Industrial Zones for Food Production","Establish economic corridors and industrial zones to support food production for import substitution.",""]],"73":[[1,"13","9","Increased Investment in Economic Sector Activities","The MTDP III intends to boost the economy by investing more in the economic sector activities to generate adequate revenues.",""],[1,"21","1","Economic Stimulus Packages for Government Investment","The Plan will intensify the Government Investments through Economic Stimulus Packages (ESP)",""],[1,"21","3","Strategic Reallocation of Capital Investment Budget","The achievement of the MTDP III targets requires a strategic shift in Capital Investment Budget Allocations.",""],[1,"38","3","Government-Led Economic Stimulus Package","government led economic stimulus package intervention in partnership with private sector is needed for structural change in our economy",""],[1,"49","1","Revenue-Increasing Key Investments","Key investments will be implemented over the medium term to increase revenue, as shown in the table below.",""],[1,"77","4","Economic Sector Capital Investment Program","over K3 billion or 12% of total medium-term capital investment will be directed into the programs",""],[1,"77","6","Prioritized Financing of High-Return Projects","Financing projects that accrue higher rate of return will generate economic capacity to service the debt and create additional value.",""],[1,"81","2","Front-Loaded Key Investment Programme","Front-load key investments to realise the MTDP III development outcomes.",""],[1,"81","7","Economic Stimulus Package","Economic stimulus package and development of missing links in transport infrastructure will be vigorously pursued.",""]],"74":[[1,"14","9","Private Sector Investment Promotion in Renewable Sectors","To create a more attractive environment for private sector investment especially in the renewable sectors;",""],[1,"15","5","Private Sector Partnership for Economic Projects","partnerships with the private sector investors in economic projects are critical.",""],[1,"41","3","Private Sector Equity Funding Partnership","The policies focus on industries and business, particularly private sector investments in partnership with the Government through equity funding, thereby creating employment and achieving economic growth.",""],[1,"42","3","Public-Private Investment Collaboration","The Government has begun collaborating and working closely with the private sector to improve investments in the agriculture, energy, and manufacturing sectors to support the service sectors.",""],[1,"45","1","SME Growth and Direct Investment Promotion","Create wealth by promoting SME growth and attracting direct investments.",""],[1,"83","1","Private Sector Development Policy Reforms","To achieve an inclusiveness and widespread growth requires extensive policy reforms that encourage private sector development.",""],[1,"83","1","Investment in Growth Enablers","The Government is investing in key enablers and as a growth facilitator; allow an increasingly vigorous private sector to develop; and strengthen governance in interactions with the private sector.",""]],"75":[[1,"17","2","Import Reduction Strategy","Under the MTDP III, the Government will focus on: (3) reducing imports,",""],[1,"44","11","Import Substitution for Major Food Items","Reduce imports of major food items like rice, dairy, fresh produce, and meat.",""],[1,"46","5","Import Substitution Strategy","Reduction of imports require parallel import substitution strategies to replace foreign imports with domestically produced goods.",""]],"76":[[1,"46","6","Technical Personnel Import Reduction Initiative","PNG continues to rely on specific skills-set because its domestic institutions could not produce internationally competitive graduates in numbers required by specific industries.",""]],"77":[[1,"48","11","Biosecurity Standards and Institutional Capacity Enhancement","Enhance bio-security standards and capacity of PNG institutions to meet the required global standards for agriculture, fishery and other products to access the niche markets",""],[1,"48","13","Manufactured Products Quality and Standards Improvement","Improve the quality and quantity of manufactured products to meet international market standards.",""]],"78":[[1,"56","3","Public Hospital Health Care Subsidy and Antiretroviral Drug Provision","The Government subsidises health care in public hospitals, including the provision of anti-retroviral drugs for persons living with HIV/AIDS.",""],[1,"56","4","Preventive Healthcare and HIV/AIDS Support Scale-Up","the Government aims to build on its current efforts by scaling up the provision of preventative healthcare and support for HIV/AIDS, including sexually transmitted infections.",""],[1,"56","7","Expanded Program on Immunisation Strengthening","The Government will strengthen the implementation of the Expanded Program on Immunisation to reach 80 percent coverage by 2022.",""],[1,"59","13","Medical Supplies Procurement and Management Improvement","Improve the procurement and management of medical supplies.",""],[1,"60","2","National Care and Treatment Services Scale-Up","Scale up care and treatment services throughout the country.",""],[1,"60","5","HIV/AIDS Awareness and Prevention Mainstreaming","HIV/AIDS awareness and prevention to be mainstreamed in schools, workplaces and communities.",""],[1,"60","6","National Response to Reduce Gender Inequalities and HIV Vulnerability","Institutionalise national response to reduce gender inequalities that contribute to PNG's high level of vulnerability to the HIV/AIDS epidemic",""],[1,"60","12","Hygiene, Nutrition and Dietary Education Awareness Programme","Support hygiene, nutrition and dietary education, programs and awareness amongst families, households and schools.",""]],"79":[[1,"71","16","Greenhouse Gas Emissions Monitoring and Carbon Accounting System Improvement","Improve systems and inventories to monitor Green House Gas Emissions (GHG) and account for carbon emissions.",""],[1,"71","17","Climate Change Legislative and Regulatory Framework Improvement","Improve climate change legislative frameworks, policies, regulations, and standards.",""],[1,"71","18","Climate Change Mitigation Support Negotiation","Negotiate to get improved funding, technical, institutional and technology support for climate change mitigation in the country.",""],[1,"71","19","Sustainable Environment and Infrastructure Policy and Regulatory Framework","Develop policy and regulatory framework for the development of Sustainable Environment and Infrastructure - development of standards and regulations for climate-proofed and resilient infrastructure",""],[1,"72","1","Climate Change Mitigation Education and R&D Support Programme","Support educational, research and development programmes associated with mitigating Climate Change impacts and management.",""],[1,"72","3","Disaster-Prone Area Building Standards Enforcement","Implement and enforce building standards for the construction of infrastructure in disaster prone areas.",""]],"80":[[1,"73","4","Islanders Resettlement Programme","All Manam and Kadavar Islanders are resettled on the mainland.",""]],"81":[[1,"26","2","MTDP III Financing Framework","Chapter 5 focuses on the financing aspect of MTDP III, identifying the requirements and gaps in funding of capital investment in the medium term.",""],[1,"77","6","Resource Mobilization for Social and Infrastructure Projects","If internal revenue is sufficiently generated and foreign exchange issue is addressed within the first three years, the Government will secure enough resources to finance other social and infrastructure projects sufficiently to achieve the goals and targets as set out in this plan.",""],[1,"77","7","Development Project Financing from Government, Grants, Concessional Loans, PPPs, and Tax Credit Scheme Reform","Development projects will be financed mainly from GoPNG sources.",""],[1,"78","5","Full Funding of the Public Investment Program","expenditure on Public Investment Program has to be fully funded.",""],[1,"78","5","Financing of Key High-Impact Projects from External and Internal Sources","The key high-impact projects should be financed from external and internal sources, including Infrastructure Tax Credit Scheme and bringing together the efforts of Government, private sector and development partners.",""],[1,"80","2","Concessional External Budget Support Arrangements","The Government of PNG has entered into the agreement with the Asian Development Bank (ADB) for the first concessional external budget support to PNG in 2018.",""],[1,"80","2","World Bank Budget Support Arrangement Negotiations","Discussions are also underway with the World Bank (WB) to define its budget support arrangements to PNG.",""],[1,"80","5","Multi-tranche Financing Facility","The Asian Development Bank (ADB) has executed one of its highly demanded financing instruments to PNG known as the Multi-tranche Financing Facility (MFF).",""],[1,"80","6","World Bank Multiphase Programmatic Approach","Similarly, the World Bank will also be executing its Multiphase Programmatic Approach (MPA), for the first time in PNG in 2018 or 2019.",""],[1,"80","7","Continuation of Long-Term Financing Modalities and Delivery Mechanisms","The Government looks forward to continuing the long term financing modalities and delivery mechanisms in critical sectors of the MTDP III and explore similar financing instruments with its development partners to boost its economic growth potentials.",""]],"82":[[1,"78","5","Infrastructure Tax Credit Scheme","The key high-impact projects should be financed from external and internal sources, including Infrastructure Tax Credit Scheme and bringing together the efforts of Government, private sector and development partners.",""],[1,"79","3","Tax Credit Rate Increase","The tax credit rates will be increased up to 2% of assessable income.",""],[1,"79","4","Infrastructure Investment Support through ITCS","ITCS will complement the National Budget process and support implementation of key investments in infrastructure sector in the most remote regions.",""],[1,"79","5","ITCS Project Procurement through the National Procurement Commission","The projects under ITCS will be procured through the National Procurement Commission (NPC).",""],[1,"79","7","Annual Audit of ITCS Projects","The ITCS projects will be audited annually.",""],[1,"79","8","Developer Reporting Strengthening Engagement","The Government will continuously engage with the developers to strengthen the reporting aspects.",""],[1,"84","3","Corporate Social Responsibility Licensing and Tax Credit Scheme","A greater shift of Corporate Social Responsibility (CSR) of multi-national companies, the private sector, and State Owned Enterprises (SOEs) to support the Government's MTDP III priorities will be put in place with issuance of CSR License to operate and benefit from our wealth in the country.",""]],"83":[[1,"72","17","Kokoda Track Initiatives Support Programme","Support the Kokoda Track Initiatives",""]],"84":[[1,"91","13","National MTDP III and PIP Projects Data Dissemination Plan","An overall national level MTDP III and PIP projects data dissemination plan developed and implemented.",""],[1,"92","4","National Data Centre and Information System","a National Data Centre and information system shall be incrementally established, managed and up scaled to meet the increasing information needs of all stakeholders, especially the decision makers, planners and implementers.",""],[1,"92","5","National Data Centre Establishment","The National Data Centre shall serve as a repository of vital information from the Wards (e.g. record books), performance reports of Service Improvement Programmes (LLGSIPs, DSIPs, and PSIPs), Alotau Accord II reports, MTDP reports, SDGs reports, PIP projects, sector performance and budget reports, evaluation and research studies, S119 reports, and other demographic data (Figure 2).",""],[1,"97","4","M&E Report Accessibility and Centralization System","M&E reports must be made easily accessible and in a timely manner to all stakeholders, including Parliament and citizens, in accordance with the GoPNG's National Planning and Monitoring Responsibility Act 2016.",""]],"85":[[1,"94","3","Economic Interagency Monitoring and Evaluation Committee","the Economic Interagency M&E Committee (EIMEC), the coordinating mechanism for economic growth strategy monitoring and reporting needs to be established.",""],[1,"94","3","Macroeconomic Policy Review Function","The EIMEC shall take the lead in reviewing the PNG macroeconomic policy, when deemed necessary.",""],[1,"94","3","Government Revenue, Expenditure, and Debt Performance Assessment","The Departments of Treasury and Finance will be charged in assessing the performance of the Government's strategies for revenue generation, expenditure and debt management.","Departments of Treasury and Finance"],[1,"94","3","Monetary and Financial Sector Stability Oversight","The BPNG will ensure that the monetary and financial sectors remain stable.","BPNG"],[1,"94","3","Macroeconomic Target Monitoring and Growth Strategy Review","DNPM will monitor the achievement of the macroeconomic targets and the review of associated growth strategies in MTDP III.","DNPM"],[1,"94","3","External Trade Target Monitoring and Reporting","The Department of Trade and Commerce (DoTC) will be charged in monitoring and reporting external trade targets, particularly exports of goods and services.","Department of Trade and Commerce (DoTC)"],[1,"94","3","Quarterly Export Tracking Reporting","Export updates will be reported to the EIMEC and will be reflected in the PNG quarterly export tracking report.",""]],"86":[[1,"96","4","Sub-national Service Delivery Data and M&E System","Provinces, districts and local authorities shall work and/or recommend to DNPM how the service delivery data will link with the national data centre/ DNPM sector information system.",""],[1,"96","5","MTDP III Monitoring and Evaluation Implementation Support","Development partners, private sector, churches and civil society play a significant role in the MTDP III M&E implementation.",""],[1,"96","6","Community Participation in MTDP Monitoring and Service Information","Communities have a stake in making sure that the MTDP M&E is producing good- quality information, thereby ensuring that they receive the services they need.",""],[1,"96","6","Community Access to Service Delivery Information","They also have a role in making sure that government and other service providers are providing them with information on the services being offered in their community, as well as service delivery (health, education, etc.,) statistics, so that they can know that their needs are being met, or can use the information to advocate, if their needs are not being met.",""]],"87":[[1,"97","2","National Planning Act Reform on Agency Performance Sanctions and Rewards","During the MTDP III implementation period, the National Planning Act needs to be revisited to introduce necessary reforms on appropriate sanctions for underperforming agencies, as well as rewards system for outstanding agencies, to further strengthen and enforce M&E and reporting process associated with the MTDP implementation.",""],[1,"97","2","DNPM Enforcement Powers for M&E Compliance","Further, DNPM, as a planning and monitoring department shall be empowered and authorised to exercise disciplinary action or suspend funding allocation for non- compliant State agencies on M&E and reporting matters.",""],[1,"97","6","Public Finance Accountability and Sanctions Enforcement","All public institutions at national and sub-national levels must be held accountable for the use of resources under the Public Finance (Management) Act (PFMA).",""],[1,"98","2","Performance Contract Accountability and Incentive Scheme","All senior managers, executive officers, or project managers must be held accountable for the use of resources set out in their respective performance contracts.",""],[1,"99","2","Anti-Corruption Initiative Strengthening Strategy","The Office of the Ombudsman will implement strategies to improve anti-corruption initiatives.","Office of the Ombudsman"],[1,"99","2","Audit and Enforcement of AFMA and Auditing Rules","The Office of the Auditor General will spearhead the review and strict enforcement of the AFMA and auditing rules and regulations, and ensure that big ticket projects are physically and financially audited and reported on an annual basis.","Office of the Auditor General"],[1,"99","2","Protection of Key Government Programmes and Investments","It will also ensure that key programmes and investments of the government are secured and protected, and issues relating to the swift and fair administration of justice are improved.",""]],"88":[[1,"91","18","Gender-Responsive Monitoring and Evaluation Integration","Gender equality and equity considerations are to be included as integral parts of all M&E activities and this will be measured through performance indicators related to gender equity and female empowerment; and wherever possible, indicators will be disaggregated by sex.",""],[1,"91","18","Gender Mainstreaming in Assessments and Data Collection","Assessments, evaluations, studies, and other data collection efforts will be required to have integrated gender considerations so that activities will be",""],[1,"101","2","Marketing and Communication Strategy for Development Plan Transparency","The inclusion of the marketing and communication strategy in MTDP III promotes a pro- disclosure culture for more transparency in the implementation of development plans.",""],[1,"101","3","MTDP III Stakeholder Awareness and Information Campaign","create awareness on and inform all stakeholders on MTDP III;",""],[1,"102","9","Radio and Television Broadcast Outreach","Radio and Television broadcast through use of programmes and advertisements.",""],[1,"102","9","Radio and Television Talkback Shows","Talkback shows on both mediums will also be conducted;",""],[1,"102","13","Official DNPM Website Information Portal","The official DNPM website where all MTDP III background and up to date information will be made available online.",""],[1,"103","4","Regional Development Forums","Regional Development Forums.",""],[1,"103","4","Public Communication on Implementation Progress and Resource Allocation","Newspaper, TV and radio talk back show to highlight key achievements; Regional and National Forums to inform on implementation progress and resource allocation.",""],[1,"103","4","Workshops","Workshops.",""],[1,"103","15","Public Communication Campaign on Key Achievements","Newspaper, TV and radio talk back show to highlight key achievements.",""]],"89":[[2,"10","1","MTDP III Priority Programs and Projects Investment","The Government will work towards achieving the MTDP III priorities by investing in key programs and projects to stimulate economic growth.",""],[2,"10","2","Five Year Strategic Investment Plan","the Government of Papua New Guinea has formulated the Five Year Strategic Investment Plan which will continue to build and consolidate the foundation for inclusive and sustainable economic growth for the present and future generations.",""],[2,"10","3","Investment Plan Implementation","The Government will work closely with all the Development Partners, the Private Sector, Civil Society Organizations and the Churches to successfully implement this Investment Plan.",""],[2,"10","3","Consistent Funding for the Investment Plan","It is critical for the Government to fund the investment plan consistently in the next five years to achieve tangible results.",""]],"90":[[2,"48","2","Free Primary Health Care Policy","PNG aims to improve the health indicators through implementation of the free health care policy; subsidized specialized health care; strengthening of health service with strong efficient system for the health workforce, financing, information, medical supplies, leadership, and governance and upgrading of district hospitals in accordance with population size and geographical requirements and to sustain them over the long term.",""],[2,"48","2","Subsidized Specialized Health Care","PNG aims to improve the health indicators through implementation of the free health care policy; subsidized specialized health care; strengthening of health service with strong efficient system for the health workforce, financing, information, medical supplies, leadership, and governance and upgrading of district hospitals in accordance with population size and geographical requirements and to sustain them over the long term.",""],[2,"48","2","Health System Strengthening and Governance Reform","PNG aims to improve the health indicators through implementation of the free health care policy; subsidized specialized health care; strengthening of health service with strong efficient system for the health workforce, financing, information, medical supplies, leadership, and governance and upgrading of district hospitals in accordance with population size and geographical requirements and to sustain them over the long term.",""],[2,"48","2","District Hospital Upgrading Programme","PNG aims to improve the health indicators through implementation of the free health care policy; subsidized specialized health care; strengthening of health service with strong efficient system for the health workforce, financing, information, medical supplies, leadership, and governance and upgrading of district hospitals in accordance with population size and geographical requirements and to sustain them over the long term.",""],[2,"48","2","District and Provincial Hospital Rehabilitation Programme","The government over the medium term will upgrade and rehabilitate the Districts and Provincial Hospitals and commence the construction of the Central Province Hospital.",""],[2,"48","2","Central Province Hospital Construction","The government over the medium term will upgrade and rehabilitate the Districts and Provincial Hospitals and commence the construction of the Central Province Hospital.",""],[2,"48","2","Angau and Port Moresby Heart and Cancer Unit Upgrades","Due to the increasing rates in lifestyle diseases and cancer related deaths nationwide, the Government will improve the Angau and Port Moresby Heart and Cancer Units to address these issues.",""],[2,"49","23","Health Service Delivery Model and Mechanism Improvement","Improve health service delivery model and mechanisms",""],[2,"49","33","Stakeholder Partnership and Coordination Strengthening","Strengthen partnerships and coordination with stakeholders",""],[2,"49","43","Establishment of Cancer Units at Angau and PMGH","5. Establishment of Cancer Units at Angau and PMGH",""],[2,"49","48","Area Medical Stores Upgrade and Rehabilitation","4 Area Medical Stores upgraded and rehabilitated",""],[2,"50","6","Establishment of Provincial Transit Medical Facilities","Establishment of Provincial Transit Medical Facilities",""],[2,"50","12","Provincial Hospitals Upgrade Program","Provincial Hospitals Upgrade Program",""]],"91":[[2,"74","1","National Housing Policy Review","Therefore, the Government will focus on reviewing the National Housing Policy ensuring that housing is made accessible and affordable.",""],[2,"74","13","National Housing Strategy","Formulate a National Housing Strategy and implement it",""],[2,"74","14","House Sales and Rental Price Regulation","Regulate house sales and rental prices (ICCC, etc.)",""],[2,"74","15","Housing Subsidy for Low- and Middle-Income Groups","Subsidize housing for low to middle income groups",""],[2,"74","16","First-Time Homeowner Housing Loan Subsidy","Subsidize housing loans for first time home owners",""],[2,"74","17","Private Sector Housing Construction Facilitation","Government agencies lead in facilitating private sector housing construction",""],[2,"74","18","National Housing Policy Review","Review the National Housing Policy",""],[2,"74","19","Housing Strategy Formulation and Implementation","Formulate and implement the housing strategy",""],[2,"74","20","Establish National Housing Database","3. Establish National Housing Database",""]],"92":[[2,"75","1","National Water, Sanitation and Hygiene Policy","In responding to the low proportion of the population having access to water and sanitation services, the National Government developed and launched the National Water, Sanitation and Hygiene (WaSH) Policy 2015-2030.",""],[2,"76","12","National Water, Sanitation and Hygiene Authority Establishment","Establish National Water, Sanitation and Hygiene Authority to coordinate the water & sanitation services",""],[2,"76","13","Rural WaSH Service Expansion Program","WaSH program to provide safe water and improved sanitation services to all rural households and business houses",""],[2,"76","14","Urban Safe Water and Sanitation Service Provision","Water PNG to provide safe water and improved sanitation services for all urban households and business houses",""],[2,"76","15","Safe Water and Improved Sanitation for Health and Education Institutions","Water PNG to provide safe water and improved sanitation services for all health and education institutions in the country",""],[2,"76","16","Establish National Water, Sanitation and Hygiene Authority","Establish National Water, Sanitation and Hygiene Authority to coordinate the water and sanitation services",""],[2,"76","17","Safe Water and Improved Sanitation Service Expansion","2. Provide safe water and improved sanitation services to all households, businesses and the population",""],[2,"76","18","Safe Water and Sanitation Services for Public Institutions","Provide safe water and sanitation services to all public (government) institutions and facilities",""],[2,"76","21","Port Moresby Sewerage System Improvement Project","Port Moresby Sewerage System Improvement Project",""]],"93":[[1,"99","2","Law and Justice Sector Coordination Mechanism for Public Order and Justice","The Law and Justice Sector will provide the mechanism for ensuring that the law and order challenges, including violent gang related crimes, tribal fighting and electoral violence which are threats to peace, stability and economic growth are mitigated and addressed.","Law and Justice Sector"],[2,"79","8","Crime Prevention Strategy Development","Develop crime prevention strategies to curb the crime prevalence issues",""],[2,"79","9","Communication and Information Management Systems Strengthening","Strengthen the communication and information management systems",""],[2,"79","10","Police-Stakeholder Partnership Arrangements","Strengthen partnership arrangements between police and interested stakeholders including private sector and development partners.",""],[2,"79","11","Participatory Community-Based Law and Justice Strengthening","Improve and enhance participatory-based approaches at the community to strengthen the processes of law and justice.",""]],"94":[[2,"83","2","Government Governance and Revenue Generation Programs","Direct Government interventions through programs and projects at both the national and sub-national levels to enhance performance in the spectrum of governance, accountability, capacity building, compliance and revenue generation initiatives will be implemented in the medium term to address these issues.",""],[2,"84","5","Independent Commission Against Corruption Establishment","Pass the bill to establish the Independent Commission Against Corruption.",""],[2,"84","6","Fiscal Planning and Expenditure Management Strengthening","Strengthen fiscal planning and expenditure management by adhering to principles laid out in the medium-term fiscal strategies.",""],[2,"84","8","National Procurement Commission Establishment","2. Establish a National Procurement Commission",""],[2,"84","21","Replacement of Ageing Tax Collection System","Replacement of Ageing Tax Collection System",""]],"95":[[2,"84","3","Procurement and Service Delivery Mechanism Strengthening","Improve and strengthen procurement and service delivery mechanism.",""],[2,"110","13","Regulatory Framework Improvement and Implementation","Improve and implement regulatory frameworks.",""],[2,"110","16","Procurement and Service Delivery Mechanism Strengthening","Improve and strengthen procurement and service delivery mechanisms.",""]],"96":[[2,"123","3","Community Health Post Rehabilitation and Feedback Mechanism","Working closely with District Administrators facilitates feedback and rehabilitation of community health posts in remote villages.",""]]}});